{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200185-brilliantrain-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought","id":1200185,"title":"BrilliantRain reads Dragon-Blooded: What Fire Has Wrought","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-27T12:36:22-07:00","id":1200185,"title":"BrilliantRain reads Dragon-Blooded: What Fire Has Wrought","content":"So, I\u2019m not promising to do this for every book, or even to be really in depth on this one. But I\u2019ve got the time to go a bit in depth on this first chunk anyway.<br /> <br /> Like the Sworn Fellowship we start with.<br /> <br /> The morality that we get from the unnamed pair of Anathema is a nice touch too. <br /> <br /> The whole \u201cLookshy is there to prevent people from seceding which the Anathema are provoking\u201d thing is interesting. It makes things more complex, since, even in their point of view, they have to acknowledge that the Anathema aren\u2019t utter monsters.<br /> <br /> Silver ring? Do Night Castes have a silver ring now and I just never noticed?<br /> <br /> ....or is this a Solar/Lunar pair?<br /> <br /> Ok, it might help things be less confusing if she called out that there was a Silver Anathema there too. Or mentioned an Ogre or something other than just going \u201cAnathema\u201d and \u201cWretched.\u201d <br /> <br /> Something.<br /> <br /> Anyway.<br /> <br /> <br /> Introduction looks good.<br /> <br /> Getting enthused by the info about the rest of the book.<br /> <br /> Ok, yes, I admit that I skip the Lexicon. If any of my questions later on are answered right here, you have my permission to mock me. But, honestly, I know enough of these terms well enough by now that I don\u2019t really need this.<br /> <br /> That said, in passing, I noted the Secondary Schools entry and I\u2019m wondering what originally elevated those schools to prominence in the first place and, if someone wanted to build or elevate a 5th school of equal stature, how they might go about doing that. I hope there might be some discussion here in the history section.<br /> <br /> <br /> I like the suggested resources. <br /> <br /> Yeah, I think not mentioning Game of Thrones and Avatar would have gotten complaints.<br /> <br /> .....And now I\u2019m imagining Game of Avatar. I bet there were a bunch of points during the Fire Nation conquering the world or the history of the Earth Kingdom that could be turned into a large scale political/martial conflict between cutthroat nobility.<br /> <br /> Admittedly, I\u2019ve not read/watched GoT, but I\u2019ve absorbed a rough impression of what it\u2019s about via osmosis.<br /> <br /> I also need to go watch season 3 of Korra. <br /> <br /> ...oh, is there a good recap of season 2 anywhere for people who are a little lost going into season 3 but can\u2019t stomach actually watching season 2? Asking for a friend.<br /> <br /> Anyway.<br /> <br /> Hm! Scarlet Empress!<br /> <br /> ....Is that the Magistrate from the Aspect books in her bed? I\u2019ve forgotten her name right now, but I\u2019ll look it up later.<br /> <br /> Interesting picture this paints of her. Thanks Neall!<br /> <br /> ........Ok, yes, I admit I\u2019m now rabidly curious what the Hearthstone of the Imperial Manse/Sword of Heaven does and exactly why the Empress needs Solars. I will grant that the implication of \u201cThe Scarlet Empress is feeding Solar Exalted to the Imperial Manse in order to sustain her control over it and, by extension, her empire\u201d is pretty clear, but I want details, man! Details!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-27T12:55:10-07:00","id":1200194,"title":"","content":"Hmm a 5th School? What about a School of the Arts! Pumping out the best Musicians, Painters, and Smiths in the Realm!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-27T13:12:30-07:00","id":1200200,"title":"","content":"How does anyone have the book already? I thought the kickstarted just started?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-27T13:19:19-07:00","id":1200203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200185-brilliantrain-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1200200#post1200200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does anyone have the book already? I thought the kickstarted just started?</div> </div> </div> </div>The first backer update (which's for backers only) has a preview PDF of the Introduction and Chapters 1 and 2. The rest of the book will be released in chunks during the KS each Tuesday.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-27T13:19:31-07:00","id":1200204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200185-brilliantrain-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1200200#post1200200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does anyone have the book already? I thought the kickstarted just started?</div> </div> </div> </div>No one has the book. There are manuscript previews being posted for backers, as they\u2019ve done for the last several kickstarters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-27T13:20:38-07:00","id":1200205,"title":"","content":"Ok, dont have mine yet. Though i did just back","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-27T13:22:42-07:00","id":1200206,"title":"","content":"You\u2019ll have to go to the Kickstarter page and click the \u201cUpdates\u201d tab. The first update has the link to the first preview. As you are now a backer, you\u2019ll get emails about updates as they\u2019re released from now on, but you don\u2019t get email notifications of updates released before you pledged.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-27T13:44:02-07:00","id":1200214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200185-brilliantrain-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought#post1200185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, it might help things be less confusing if she called out that there was a Silver Anathema there too. Or mentioned an Ogre or something other than just going \u201cAnathema\u201d and \u201cWretched.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this. Anathema are Anathema. It doesn't matter if they're Solar or Lunar. Bad is bad. Nice, simple, effective way of teaching society.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-27T13:46:08-07:00","id":1200215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200185-brilliantrain-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought#post1200185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hm! Scarlet Empress!<br /> <br /> ....Is that the Magistrate from the Aspect books in her bed? I\u2019ve forgotten her name right now, but I\u2019ll look it up later.<br /> <br /> Interesting picture this paints of her. Thanks Neall!<br /> <br /> ........Ok, yes, I admit I\u2019m now rabidly curious what the Hearthstone of the Imperial Manse/Sword of Heaven does and exactly why the Empress needs Solars. I will grant that the implication of \u201cThe Scarlet Empress is feeding Solar Exalted to the Imperial Manse in order to sustain her control over it and, by extension, her empire\u201d is pretty clear, but I want details, man! Details!</div> </div> </div> </div>This was probably my single favorite part of the overall preview thus far as well.<br /> <br /> I'm with you on the details thing, too. While I can appreciate &quot;it is what it needs to be for your table&quot;, stuff like this where it just gives tantalizing hints make me want something concrete. I'm hoping there's more on this in <b>The Realm</b>, if it isn't in the DB book proper.<br /> <br /> And I'm pretty sure that you're right that it was Tepet Elana in there. About the only talking points about her that weren't present was her haircut and the discount Cloud Strife buster sword of a daiklave she preferred in the art. lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1817-opmegs","name":"OpMegs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1817_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-27T14:09:11-07:00","id":1200221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200185-brilliantrain-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought#post1200185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">exactly why the Empress needs Solars. I will grant that the implication of \u201cThe Scarlet Empress is feeding Solar Exalted to the Imperial Manse in order to sustain her control over it and, by extension, her empire\u201d is pretty clear, but I want details, man! Details!</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bIn fairness, that's been a detail of the Scarlet Empress' relationship with the Sword since First Edition. Any time that she disappeared in that manner romanticised into her wandering the Blessed Isle disguised as a commoner, she was generally performing maintenance rites, which included feeding the Anathema to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-27T15:23:02-07:00","id":1200237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200185-brilliantrain-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1200214#post1200214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like this. Anathema are Anathema. It doesn't matter if they're Solar or Lunar. Bad is bad. Nice, simple, effective way of teaching society.</div> </div> </div> </div>While that might be useful for indoctrination purposes, it doesn\u2019t help as much when the Wyld Hunt comes in loaded for a Lunar sorcerer and runs into a Dawn meat grinder because the locals didn\u2019t know the difference.<br /> <br /> Either way, I expect an Exalted Immaculate Monk to know the different types of Anathema, especially since she mentions a Wretched specifically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-27T22:06:52-07:00","id":1200352,"title":"","content":"I love that you guys paint in cool mythical tidbits everywhere you can. In fact, imma quote this section because it\u2019s awesome:<br /> <br /> \u201cFragments of that era still linger in hidden corners of the world. The art of the Zebremani people of the South traditionally depicts their heroes as crowned with fire or mantled with storms. The vast undersea palace ruled by the storm mother Konobala was once home to the Water Aspect princes of the Nine-Eyed Throne. The Sliver-of-a-Dream Pagoda, perched high upon the sheer southern face of Wujun Mountain, is still accessible only by the handholds that the hermit Love-is-Lightning carved into the living rock with his bare hands.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> The Shogunate: <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tragedy_of_the_commons\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tragedy_of_the_commons</a><br /> <br /> Nice that you called that out.<br /> <br /> Really, why couldn\u2019t they have a Council or a Senate or /something/? Why does one person gotta be in charge?<br /> <br /> I suppose they were used to having a military style organization with a pretty strict chain of command.<br /> <br /> I hope the Sidereals book goes into whether or not they think the Shogunate was a preventable failure or not.<br /> <br /> Basic history recap is well done.<br /> <br /> Liking the other DB groups and things.<br /> <br /> Hmm... a Census! So about 25,000 DBs all over Creation then, vs. 300 Solars, 400 Lunars, and 100 Sidereals and then all the other Exalts.<br /> <br /> Given those numbers, I think DBs kind of have to be the largest Exalt type. Even if there are still 1,000 Alchemicals, that\u2019s.... yeah. It kinda brings home just how ...I don\u2019t want to say common or omnipresent, but, how compared to the other Exalted, they\u2019re just so widespread.<br /> <br /> I gotta say, I love the writing. Very evocative.<br /> <br /> I hope we get a dedicated book about the Realm Schools at some point. <br /> <br /> I have to admit that I find the characters of people who apparently failed to Exalt interesting. Someone who apparently Exalted as a DB at age 22 or so would be an interesting plot seed. Did they manage to fake it with some other source of power (and now a Lunar is well ensconced in DB society)? Did they manage to find an external trigger for their latent potential? Did the pilgrimage to the Caul help them somehow? Lots of fun potential there.<br /> <br /> Heck, even just the potential for a person to fail at that, get posted somewhere in the threshold, and then Exalt as an Anathema some years later is interesting. Because there\u2019s gonna be a part of you that\u2019s hella amazed by what you can do now and how much more awesome you are than the DBs....and another part that still feels bad about failing your parents and is wondering if you\u2019ll be able to kill your relatives when they come hunting you.<br /> <br /> ......<br /> <br /> .....Ok, fine, these are dynasts we\u2019re talking about. I\u2019m sure some of them are positively salivating for a chance to murder all those jerks they grew up with and everything. But still.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.giantitp.com/comics/oots0603.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.giantitp.com/comics/oots0603.html</a><br /> <br /> Incidentally, I do like Sesus Rafara\u2019s character and I\u2019m honestly hoping that someone manages to sneak in a note that her mother died of a \u201centirely normal accident\u201d into canon somewhere.<br /> <br /> Anyway, where was I?<br /> <br /> Nice sidebar on the Immaculate Texts. Knowing that, for the most part, they weren\u2019t written whole cloth by Sidereals helps take it more seriously.<br /> <br /> Love the exaltation stories.<br /> <br /> Very interesting notes on the relationship between Aspect and Personality.<br /> <br /> So, the lazy patrician\u2019s daughter after exalting as an Air aspect, might find a new appreciation for intellectual pursuits and develop some zeal for pursuing them... or might find that things come so much more easily to her that she can fulfill expectations with even less work now? Does that sound right?<br /> <br /> Hmm... I\u2019m going to need to revisit some NPC personalities in light of these Aspect tendencies. It should help them become more round characters though.<br /> <br /> Ok, seriously, Heptagram book. Because I just know that people reading this section are gonna wanna do Realm School Games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-28T06:37:31-07:00","id":1200404,"title":"","content":"How many you imagine exist among the Dragonblooded of the Forest Witches, do you think due to their secret nature they aren't part of the estimated census numbers given, or do you think they are part of the Outcaste number.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-28T06:54:51-07:00","id":1200410,"title":"","content":"I lump them in as an outcaste group. There's probably a couple hundred of htem, but they don't feel like a nation state in the way the Houses each do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-28T08:04:13-07:00","id":1200432,"title":"","content":"Nation-state feels like the wrong term to use. &quot;Nation&quot; there seems like more of a tribal, ethnic term. On a few counts, the Houses seem to be built up in a manner reminiscent of sovereign tribal groups that you get, as an example, in some African countries.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T01:52:48-07:00","id":1200740,"title":"","content":"You never actually use the word \u201cstubborn\u201d when talking about Earth Aspects. Impressive.<br /> <br /> So, the failure modes for the aspects are: dreamer out of touch with reality, stubborn reactionary jerk, spoiled brat, chronic backstabbing syndrome, and free love hippie?<br /> <br /> My essence is a fever and the only cure is more Cowbell.<br /> <br /> The prestige spread puts a pleasant face on empire, but doesn\u2019t avoid mentioning some uncomfortable aspects. Which is probably about right.<br /> <br /> Lookshy\u2019s entry is about as accurate, isn\u2019t it?<br /> <br /> So, how will they know the worthy shogun when she arrives? Is there a Daiklave in a rock somewhere? Also, isn\u2019t the Shogun just the military commander? So, then, isn\u2019t the person with the biggest army and best tactics automatically the rightful Shogun?<br /> <br /> I am not familiar with a meaning of \u201ctempered\u201d that includes \u201csquandered on petty pissing matches.\u201d<br /> <br /> So, is Prasad well covered in this book, or should we be expecting a Stretch Goal for more Prasad in the companion?<br /> <br /> This feels a lot like India to me, which is intentional, I\u2019m sure.<br /> <br /> Visit exotic places! Meet interesting people! Conquer one and kill the other!<br /> <br /> I assume that the Realm couldn\u2019t project enough force to actually bring this place into the full and proper fold. I find myself wondering how Chejop feels about this place.<br /> <br /> This has been your reminder that the Forest Witches are hella weird.<br /> <br /> ...Yeah, being an Outcaste is kinda nice. No one is going to call a Wyld Hunt on you, but you\u2019ve got enough of an edge to handle most people that might come your way. The real problem is when you\u2019re forced to fight outside your weight class and you probably will be.<br /> <br /> Well, you also don\u2019t usually get to recline on a jade pleasure couch in between snorting heroin mixed with gold dust off a beautiful slave\u2019s taut stomach like they do in the Realm, but you can\u2019t have everything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T06:15:17-07:00","id":1200777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200185-brilliantrain-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1200740#post1200740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, how will they know the worthy shogun when she arrives? Is there a Daiklave in a rock somewhere? Also, isn\u2019t the Shogun just the military commander? So, then, isn\u2019t the person with the biggest army and best tactics automatically the rightful Shogun?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, like obviously a <i>worthy </i>shogun will be one to restore the last legitimate successor to the shogunate, aka Lookshy, to the old shogunate's full glory.<br /> <br /> \u200bSomeone who demands Lookshy capituate, then <i>fails </i>to conquor the city when they refuse, is clearly not a rightful Shogun.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T06:18:35-07:00","id":1200778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200185-brilliantrain-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1200740#post1200740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, is Prasad well covered in this book, or should we be expecting a Stretch Goal for more Prasad in the companion?</div> </div> </div> </div>It gets a writeup in The Realm; dunno about the companion, we'll have to see.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T08:21:10-07:00","id":1200812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200185-brilliantrain-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1200740#post1200740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This feels a lot like India to me, which is intentional, I\u2019m sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>I got a lot of the same feeling as well. I get a feeling of a lot of the 'Empire ruled by outsiders gone native' that reminds me of the Mughals, or even the remnants of Alexander's empire in India. That with a little dose of British Colonialism in the subcontinent.<br /> <br /> I've already been plundering Mughal prince's names for characters from the area.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1982-spacepup","name":"Spacepup","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T10:52:41-07:00","id":1200876,"title":"","content":"Chapter 2<br /> <br /> ...I have an Eclipse Caste merchant PC who wishes she was that awesome. Fortunately, she has a Dawn Caste bodyguard who can be that awesome for her.<br /> <br /> What does failure look like for a house? Tepet?<br /> <br /> Never have the parallels between the Shogunate and the modern Realm been more clear. I suppose Lookshy might claim that this will \u201ctemper\u201d the Realm into something better.<br /> <br /> I feel like we get a better sense of motion here, with the Realm as a dynamic entity. Just because there are ten-ish houses now, doesn\u2019t mean there always will be and certainly doesn\u2019t mean there always were. Even the fact that Households can rise in importance or fade away is a very useful note.<br /> <br /> Discussing the privileges and duties of the House Matriarch is useful here. One has to wonder what happens when a Matriarch becomes selfish or indolent. Well, ok, I\u2019m sure they get deposed sooner or later or the House falls apart, but I doubt it happens quickly and the lead up to it should be pretty interesting. Why is the house Matriarch doing this? Can she hide it successfully? Are other family members hiding her weaknesses and, if so, how long can they keep doing it or are they sharpening the knives?<br /> <br /> Good note on names.<br /> <br /> Good info on land holdings.<br /> <br /> I wonder just how badly you have to screw up to have the Matriarch take away your artifact. Yes, it says they mostly don\u2019t do that, but there\u2019s gotta be a point where they at least threaten to take it away.<br /> <br /> Maybe call it House Heraldry?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T13:59:13-07:00","id":1200971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200185-brilliantrain-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1200876#post1200876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Chapter 2<br /> I feel like we get a better sense of motion here, with the Realm as a dynamic entity. Just because there are ten-ish houses now, doesn\u2019t mean there always will be and certainly doesn\u2019t mean there always were. Even the fact that Households can rise in importance or fade away is a very useful note.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, although that was the case in 2nd ed it wasn't really presented well, and they never talked much about how things were different.<br /> I liked, for example, the note that a few hundred years ago the Empress repealed the benefits and privelages of the Shogunate Gentes, implying that in the first few hundred years the Realm was quite different, with Shogunate Gentes being a significant force.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T15:38:15-07:00","id":1201028,"title":"","content":"...So I\u2019m actually a bit embarrassed by how long it took me to twig to the fact that the chapter 2 opening fiction plays in to the Realm stereotypes perfectly. <br /> <br /> It has an irrational and emotional male stage a rash attack upon a woman in a stupid attempt to improve his own status, while the poised and careful woman simply lets him demonstrate his unfit state until she gets tired of humoring him and lays him out on the ground without even spilling her drink, therby demonstrating just how much more controlled, careful, temperate, and intelligent she is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T17:59:14-07:00","id":1201092,"title":"","content":"And now, the houses.<br /> <br /> <br /> House Cathak<br /> <br /> So, the houses are Primordials now? Kimbery should sue.<br /> <br /> Based on this description, I\u2019m imagining ideal Samurai or perfect swashbucklers from this house. People who are both deadly and cultured. Cyrano de Bergerac. The Lion Clan.<br /> <br /> Silken Blade Codex<br /> <br /> ...I kinda wanna read a Realm romance novel now. The Cathak officer of 100 years, battleworn, but articulate and passionate (and athletic) looking for a new young husband sounds much more appealing than the aged masses of flab that young women are always in danger of being married to in our romance novels.<br /> <br /> ...what about male scions of the house? ...oh, right, they\u2019ll be sent away to other houses by the time they\u2019re in their 20s, so they don\u2019t really matter.<br /> <br /> I wonder if the bookish accountant type husbandos have to deal with ridicule and stuff too? Looks like probably not. Which is a fair point. Experienced officers understand the importance of logistics.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhoever wins the Realm will also gain my hand in marriage!\u201d And now everyone in Creation is interested.<br /> <br /> So, House Cathak has, basically, the strongest army in the Realm right now. Between their strategic genius and the fact that they\u2019ve got Eight Legions, anyone would need to be crazy to fight them...especially if they can get them on their side.<br /> <br /> Very nice plan Cainan.<br /> <br /> House Sesus will be interesting to compare to this one. Tepet too.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m really getting curious about Ragara.<br /> <br /> Fajad sounds familiar. Was it in the Corebook? I\u2019ll need to check. It also sounds interesting.<br /> <br /> Hmm! Cathak herself. Getting bios on all the founders will be cool.<br /> <br /> So, he was appointed Matriarch by Cathak herself. Interesting.<br /> <br /> I wonder how she was poisoned.<br /> <br /> So....smuggling a peach of immortality to Cainan isn\u2019t an option?<br /> <br /> Elanda sounds potentially useful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T21:54:23-07:00","id":1201140,"title":"","content":"Going a little out of order because one of my players wanted to discuss House Ledaal, so I had to go ahead and read it.<br /> <br /> House Ledaal<br /> <br /> Hm! This is pretty interesting. Very evocative and brings forward the \u201cintellectual house\u201d in a whole new way. Bringing out the whole Monster Hunter aspect that they have seems good.<br /> <br /> I like it.<br /> <br /> .....and of course disagreements over resources are causing problems here too.<br /> <br /> I gotta ask, is the DB great curse that fellowships eventually break down and turn on themselves or is that just human nature?<br /> <br /> Why do people marry into this house? Because they have a bookish son they can\u2019t otherwise get rid of? Because they want to show support for the Realm in general? Because they have an Anathema problem they need solved? Because they need to know something that Ledaal knows?<br /> <br /> Ok, I bet that, just cause they focus on monsters, doesn\u2019t mean they don\u2019t play politics at all. They have to have resources and satrapies and people in positions of authority and everything, so marrying in for all that jazz is also reasonable. Especially if the Empress regarded them as highly dependable and gave them choice places to exploit as a result.<br /> <br /> Still, I\u2019m not surprised they\u2019re scrambling for alliances now, just to make sure the Realm doesn\u2019t fall apart.<br /> <br /> So, when her mother consorted with Anathema to try to take over the world, she just went and killed her. That\u2019s pretty impressive and kinda sad.<br /> <br /> I am now imagining Batman as a Ledaal. Or at least one of those brooding demon hunters in the long cloak and crossbow.<br /> <br /> ....ok, I grant that there is a point here. Going after Thorns or retaking the Caul or dealing the deathblow to the Bull and his forces or going after Perfect Soul\u2019s rogue satrapy or any of several hundred other problems... these are all existential threats to the Realm as a whole and they\u2019re all only getting worse. Another issue is that the House doesn\u2019t have our omniscient view of everything, so one important member of the house dismisses half the reports out of Thorns as obvious exaggeration while another one thinks they\u2019re underestimating the problem (and really both are technically correct) so they have different ideas about the needs of the situation, while a third agrees with the second, but thinks that Thorns is a lost cause without a unified Realm and ....yeah, ok. I can see why they\u2019re in a pickle and why the house leaders are pulling in different directions and making the problem worse.<br /> <br /> So many irons in the fire.<br /> <br /> Ledaal allying with Mnemon would be bad. For anyone who isn\u2019t the Realm.<br /> <br /> So, they\u2019ve developed a potion to temporarily boost a DB\u2019s Essence to 5 (or maybe even 6) ...but anyone who takes it will lose 50 to 100 years of life at minimum and they\u2019ll likely be crazy for the duration and impotent afterwards. And this is the best case scenario. Finding test subjects for that must have been ...complicated.<br /> <br /> ......I would know more of Perch and it\u2019s Hungry Ghost Sphinxes.<br /> <br /> Ledaal and Rowena Ravenclaw had a lot in common it sounds like.<br /> <br /> I clearly need to read the Ragara section now.<br /> <br /> Nice twist on Ledaal Kebok Coren\u2019s ancestry reveal. I could see the house ignoring that in this time of need ...and then quietly assassinating her afterwards.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T22:08:41-07:00","id":1201143,"title":"","content":"Incidentally, I think this video about the Tragedy of the Commons is pretty relevant here: <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MvXuAXSC82w\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MvXuAXSC82w</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T03:57:13-07:00","id":1201201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200185-brilliantrain-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1201092#post1201092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">So....smuggling a peach of immortality to Cainan isn\u2019t an option?</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Sure it is, technically.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Just so unlikely as to not really be something one banks their future on.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u200bThose are just about the second most valuable thing in Heaven.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200185-brilliantrain-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1201140#post1201140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I gotta ask, is the DB great curse that fellowships eventually break down and turn on themselves or is that just human nature?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there are almost seven billion humans; it's bound to be the nature of a few million of them.<br /> <br /> \u200bI think it's more about the tendency of complex systems to break down.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">yeah, ok. I can see why they\u2019re in a pickle and why the house leaders are pulling in different directions and making the problem worse.<br /> <br /> So many irons in the fire.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bRight?! This kind of strategic situation, where they're faced with a number of objectives, several contradictory, all critically important, and none with an easy answer about how to fulfil, I think that's genius for the complexity and compelling character motivation it presents. There's a concrete basis here for Realm politics, whether one is playing a Ledaal or having them as supporting or antagonistic characters, or even just in the background of a chronicle; characters having specific goals that they need to commit to and convince others of, even though it can represent a risk or a gamble or a sacrifice.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe idea of it as possible background noise particularly interesting to me, because of how it makes the setting feel alive; logically, Ledaal is going to do <i>something</i> whether the PCs are involved or not, so one can generate setting texture or potential plot hooks just from being at the margins of whatever they do. You could play a Realm game focused entirely on the interplay between three other Houses that are barely connected to Ledaal, or some other group adventuring through the Scavenger Lands, and then boom, unilateral Ledaal crusade against Thorns becomes something that is... mentioned, and it alternately serves as an interesting piece of noise or event to generate further drama.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T09:34:09-07:00","id":1201299,"title":"","content":"I loved the Cathak Social Standing section. The penultimate paragraph reads like gender-flipped stereotypical Jane Austen-type romances.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://wondrousatlas.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">Wondrous Atlas of Creation's Destiny</a> - I cohost an Exalted podcast focusing on examining the setting's lore and how to develop them into elements to use in games.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/924488-homebuilt-exalted-st-screen-reference-sheet\" target=\"_blank\">Ex3 Reference Materials</a> - currently includes an ST screen, common actions sheet, weapons reference sheet, character creation summary and mortal QCs reference sheet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/497-xerxes","name":"Xerxes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar497_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T14:24:31-07:00","id":1201412,"title":"","content":"House Cynis<br /> <br /> So, they\u2019re the Wicked Cultured house then? Are they decadent enough to create wines that pair well with specific poisons?<br /> <br /> Are they actually happy if a member of the house is happy or is that part of the act too?<br /> <br /> Hmmm.... They, like Cathak, are well positioned to be Queenmakers instead of Queens. I wonder who they\u2019ll be supporting. Alternately, I suppose they could find one of their scions who had become a Monk but who didn\u2019t actually hate their house and put them forward.<br /> <br /> ....Yeah, if they were JUST the party house they wouldn\u2019t have lasted this long. I was waiting for the other shoe to drop all through that bit about their reputation.<br /> <br /> I find myself wondering how the slaves react to the house. Do they even attempt to ensure that the skilled slaves are \u201chappy\u201d in their position or do they simply use them up as needed, confident they can always get more?<br /> <br /> I\u2019m sure that unskilled labor sucks for them, like it always does, but I could imagine skilled slaves being cared for relatively well, depending on their particular skill. Admittedly, that depends on your master and just how much reason they might have to want you productive vs in their bed.<br /> <br /> And of course they\u2019re taking ostensibly protected \u201ccitizens\u201d now.<br /> <br /> All the drugs, yes.<br /> <br /> Ok, medicine is respected enough that maybe they could put forth a relative straight laced doctor and at least not get the Immaculate Order to denounce them outright?<br /> <br /> Really, they\u2019re like if the Scorpion Clan wore the Crane Clan as a mask. <br /> <br /> What happens with Cynis, stays with Cynis.<br /> <br /> And now I\u2019m imaging a Cynis sorcerer who has several slaves, each of whom has had to memorize decades of secrets and then had Corrupted Words cast upon them to lock the secrets away until the sorcerer needs them. And maybe some kind of Working to ensure that the spell vanishes at death or something. Depends on whether they want to ensure that others don\u2019t kill them for fear of releasing the secrets or what.<br /> <br /> Oh, Mnemon is the eldest daughter now? Well, probably eldest living daughter anyway. I wonder which of them she had assassinated?<br /> <br /> I\u2019m really not fond of Mnemon. We will see if you can change my mind.<br /> <br /> Ragara is older than her, right?<br /> <br /> Hmmm... Ragara, V\u2019neef, Mnemon... Does the Empress have any other living children?<br /> <br /> Ok, so. House Cathak has the army. Cynis has the info and pleasure. Ragara has the Money.<br /> <br /> What do others have?<br /> <br /> So, Sesus is another dirty tricks house? Interesting.<br /> <br /> Sounds like Sesus and Cynis are joined at the hip. Maybe they should just try to elevate a Sesus then?<br /> <br /> Pangu sounds like a lovely place.<br /> <br /> Spider ridden Kubal? Sounds interesting.<br /> <br /> Ok, so that\u2019s why they hold on to Greyfalls. I can\u2019t help but think that there are Lunars just waiting for the Realm to abandon this place to unleash their army of beastmen and break the geomancy of one of those important manses.<br /> <br /> Ok, is it just me or is anyone else suspicious of Cynis ODing? Had Mnemon been born then? How about Ragara?<br /> <br /> Are Cynis Umara and Cynis Cerise both Exalted? Because I thought that basically never happened with twins? That might be worth making explicit in the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T19:24:59-07:00","id":1201507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200185-brilliantrain-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1201412#post1201412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, is it just me or is anyone else suspicious of Cynis ODing? Had Mnemon been born then? How about Ragara?</div> </div> </div> </div>Y'know, given the number of House founders that died gloriously in battle, my first thought on reading that was &quot;Cynis died by managing to overdose despite being an elemental demigoddess of an aspect <i>specifically known</i> to be resistant to most normal poisons. That must be the closest thing House Cynis gets to considering something a glorious death in battle.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1817-opmegs","name":"OpMegs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1817_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T19:35:33-07:00","id":1201509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200185-brilliantrain-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1201412#post1201412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ok, is it just me or is anyone else suspicious of Cynis ODing?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI thought it was a bit on the nose for a character of that temperament, but don't find it unbelievable that an Exalt could consume substances of toxic nature or quantity in pursuit of a greater high.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T20:25:27-07:00","id":1201526,"title":"","content":"Maybe I'm just paranoid after reading all that about the houses then. I just suspect that both Mnemon and Ragara want to be mommy's only child very, very badly and after reading Cynis's whole dirty tricks thing, I got a bit suspicious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T20:31:44-07:00","id":1201529,"title":"","content":"I like the idea that Cynis did OD, but it still triggered immediate fallout as though it was a blatant assassination because that's what people assumed it had to have been, including Mnemon and Ragara assuming the other one did it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T20:39:12-07:00","id":1201530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200185-brilliantrain-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1201529#post1201529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the idea that Cynis did OD, but it still triggered immediate fallout as though it was a blatant assassination because that's what people assumed it had to have been, including Mnemon and Ragara assuming the other one did it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooooh! That IS a fun take on it. I would NOT want to be the Magistrate assigned to that case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T21:22:42-07:00","id":1201535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200185-brilliantrain-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1201526#post1201526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe I'm just paranoid after reading all that about the houses then. I just suspect that both Mnemon and Ragara want to be mommy's only child very, very badly and after reading Cynis's whole dirty tricks thing, I got a bit suspicious.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the one in the whole killing their siblings thing was mostly Ragara, as Mnemon by my gathering actually while wanting to be on top, wasn't so damned sociopathic. That she has tombs for her siblings and adopted her sister into her House kind of indicate to me that while she wants the Throne, she was less in the &quot;there can be only one' thing.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T21:28:59-07:00","id":1201536,"title":"","content":"I don't think that Mnemon necessarily wants to be her mother's <i>only</i> living child, so much as she's wanting to be the dominant one. House Mnemon's writeup gives a bit more detail to a counterexample there. She's just come to the conclusion that she needs to be the dominant power with any member of her family as the only way she's going to survive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1817,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1817-opmegs","user":"OpMegs","date":". 03-31-2018, 12:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1817-opmegs","name":"OpMegs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1817_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T22:42:09-07:00","id":1201542,"title":"","content":"I'd imagine in a family like the Empress' a lot of the children were in the camp of &quot;I don't want <i> all</i> of my siblings dead. I don't think it would be too much to ask for one or two specific siblings to die though that would be nice.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T22:54:06-07:00","id":1201543,"title":"","content":"That's the bit I'm getting at though.<br /> <br /> Like, could Mnemon have been instrumental in the death of some of her siblings? Sure. Very likely actually.<br /> <br /> Was she responsible for a long line of bodies that any particular one was probably hers? That I'm more skeptical about. She seems to care about her siblings enough when they're <i>not</i> being pitched against her. Not every single solitary daughter of the Empress rises to Great House afterall. V'Neef was around while Iselsi was in decline for decades, and she was just turning 40 when she got her House. They're rivals, but I think folks like Mnemon are young enough to be pretty sure they weren't going to be heir by making sure there weren't others, and she probably was just making sure she could be around in RY 1000 and be the best candiate.<br /> <br /> This being said...none of this applies to Ragara. Dude was a socipathic asshole since 1e's take on him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-31T03:47:08-07:00","id":1201574,"title":"","content":"Is it permissible to talk about parts of the book you haven't read yet?<br /> <br /> I don't really want to, but it seems that others are edging there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-31T13:31:29-07:00","id":1201688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200185-brilliantrain-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1201574#post1201574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it permissible to talk about parts of the book you haven't read yet?<br /> <br /> I don't really want to, but it seems that others are edging there.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t really mind honestly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-31T13:36:41-07:00","id":1201689,"title":"","content":"House Mnemon<br /> <br /> Ok, we\u2019re here now. Let\u2019s see if she\u2019s still as self-centered as a top and with a delusional degree of faith in her own abilities.<br /> <br /> When they say \u201cabove reproach\u201d what does that mean exactly?<br /> <br /> So, they\u2019re the best of the best, then? What do they do to members who don\u2019t measure up?<br /> <br /> Pure blood.<br /> <br /> Ok, how exactly is Ragra still alive? Did the Empress condone him trying to assassinate his siblings? And why hasn\u2019t Mnemon killed him yet?<br /> <br /> Did the Empress plan for Mnemon and Ragara to have to get in bed together?<br /> <br /> So, has she actually reclaimed Jiara or are they still fighting there?<br /> <br /> Hmmm. Yeah, accidentally creating a Red Festival would be bad for publicity.<br /> <br /> Maybe you should try not being a jerk in order to get the peasants to love you.<br /> <br /> Since when has Peleps been an exemplar of anything?<br /> <br /> Mnemon really doesn\u2019t like to bow before anyone, does she?<br /> <br /> In light of the Cathak entry, I think she\u2019s got a decent chance of gaining their support if she can get enough of everyone else to support her.<br /> <br /> Ledaal makes sense as an ally, in view of Jiara.<br /> <br /> Immaculate Order...interesting.<br /> <br /> Huh. Not any mention of \u201cMnemon finding a Cynis on the throne blasphemous\u201d or anything, just annoyance at how much control they have over Sesus.<br /> <br /> So, bookish elder sister is annoyed that her younger sister is prettier and more popular. Interesting.<br /> <br /> Ok, I REALLY need to read the Ragara entry. Also, with just how much Ragara is calling in their debts, I kinda have to wonder why all the other houses haven\u2019t banded together to stomp it off the map and cancel all their debts that way. Or even just ...ignore the Ragara debt collection teams en mass. I suppose no-one is quite ready to upend the economy just yet.<br /> <br /> Because of course she\u2019d name a city after herself. I have to wonder if she\u2019s secretly insecure and that\u2019s why she acts like she does.<br /> <br /> Ok, Chainbright sounds spectacular.<br /> <br /> Hmm... Mnemon built tombs for her dead siblings. Interesting.<br /> <br /> I still wanna know how Ragara managed to get away with killing his siblings when other houses have been destroyed for similar offenses.<br /> <br /> I wouldn\u2019t have necessarily called it that Mnemon would have their own Las Vegas, but it\u2019s hard to be the preeminent exemplar of the Scarlet Dynasty if you ignore the court and everything.<br /> <br /> Another good point to call out how men are perceived.<br /> <br /> Paragon is as expected. Though good to call it out as a Satrapy. Though, now I\u2019m wondering what they think of the architecture of the place and how it lacks color.<br /> <br /> It sounds like her council has to walk a thin line between being \u201cyes-women\u201d and offering actually useful advice. It\u2019s kind of a pity she can\u2019t trust anyone. I\u2019ve seen a theory that Ragara destroyed her ability to trust people, which I find plausible. It makes me wonder what she would have been like had she grown up in a more nurturing environment.<br /> <br /> ....I bet she assumes she\u2019d be dead several times over by now if she hadn\u2019t become who she is. Which is also kinda sad.<br /> <br /> I almost wish that Mnemon and V\u2019Neef could have a hug and get to just be sisters for a bit. Never gonna happen, but I think they\u2019d both feel much better if they could.<br /> <br /> She WOULD have someone watching Chejop Kejak.<br /> <br /> I find myself thinking that trying to become exactly like the Scarlet Empress probably wasn\u2019t such a good idea, assuming it was intentional.<br /> <br /> Austerity. Interesting.<br /> <br /> Her sister? Hmmm...<br /> <br /> I wonder if that was kindness or a ploy to get an amazingly loyal ally? Possibly both. Alternately, Mnemon might not be able to tell anymore.<br /> <br /> A sidebar on what happens to people who don\u2019t fit in their house or don\u2019t measure up or whatever would be useful, btw. Assuming it\u2019s not discussed later anyway.<br /> <br /> Shouldn\u2019t Mnemon Pallan be discussed with his wife\u2019s House?<br /> <br /> Hollow Codex<br /> <br /> Ok, this is an interesting heresy. I\u2019m now imagining some con artists manipulating him through drug induced visions.<br /> <br /> I feel like some notes on the ones who don\u2019t measure up to Mnemon\u2019s desires might have been useful, but, given how everyone needs to measure up to their house\u2019s desires, I suppose a general section on that for everyone might be more useful.<br /> <br /> Ok, yes, I feel some sympathy for her now. I still think she\u2019d be a terrible Empress, but I\u2019ll grant that she\u2019s not an utterly unsympathetic egomaniac. So, I suppose I do still think she\u2019s as self-centered as a top and with a delusional degree of faith in her own abilities, but at least part of that comes from having been seriously hurt emotionally during her formative years and needing to appear strong afterwards, which does humanize her and makes her more sympathetic.<br /> <br /> Honestly, anyone who actually wants to be the Scarlet Empress, should probably be disqualified, because they likely only see the power, wealth, and fripperies and would be useless at actually running things. Mnemon, I will grant, is probably a capable administrator by now at least.<br /> <br /> <br /> Hmm... I just noted that we skipped Iselsi. Hmmm..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-31T13:39:37-07:00","id":1201690,"title":"","content":"We need a section on Assassination in the Realm. How condoned is it and stuff. How hidden does it need to be? Will Magistrates just look the other way if they can\u2019t prove it, but it\u2019s an open secret? How does it all work?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-31T15:08:25-07:00","id":1201713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200185-brilliantrain-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1201689#post1201689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">why hasn\u2019t Mnemon killed him yet?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThat would probably be hard in any case, but she wants him to see the downfall of everything he ever worked for first.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe you should try not being a jerk in order to get the peasants to love you.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think she's a jerk, just... severe.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe contrast between her and some other House founders puts me in mind of the difference between the Duke of Wellington and the likes of Napoleon or von Blucher; the latter were well liked among their troops, friendly, personable, subject to affectionate nicknames, whereas Wellington was stern and harsh, respected by his troops for his command prowess, but still cold.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since when has Peleps been an exemplar of anything?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bOh you'll see. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, bookish elder sister is annoyed that her younger sister is prettier and more popular. Interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI like to think of it as being more like Mnemon having drawn a lot of capital from the popular perception that she was reminiscent of the Empress, and feels threatened and undermined by the presence of somebody who does it better than she does.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because of course she\u2019d name a city after herself. I have to wonder if she\u2019s secretly insecure and that\u2019s why she acts like she does.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bHonestly, I feel as though when you're responsible for largely building or rebuilding a place, adding your name to it is not unwarranted. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still wanna know how Ragara managed to get away with killing his siblings when other houses have been destroyed for similar offenses.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which ones?<br /> <br /> \u200b(I presume that Ragara had some discretion and a secure enough position that he was able to get away with it for a while, before he ultimately crossed a line)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shouldn\u2019t Mnemon Pallan be discussed with his wife\u2019s House?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bNah, married men are still considered scions of their birth House. I see it as a useful way of categorizing them for showing how they make forays into other Houses.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, anyone who actually wants to be the Scarlet Empress, should probably be disqualified, because they likely only see the power, wealth, and fripperies and would be useless at actually running things. Mnemon, I will grant, is probably a capable administrator by now at least.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, that's how I would have viewed previous Mnemon, but I think the current one would actually try and implement policies based on her religious ideology.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-01T17:46:27-07:00","id":1202071,"title":"","content":"House Nellens<br /> <br /> I always liked them. I suppose I like underdogs.<br /> <br /> The conclave is old, but I like that they\u2019ve given everyone specific roles. I\u2019m glad everyone is getting that this time around.<br /> <br /> Sounds like they marry for love even less than Ledaal does. <br /> <br /> It also sounds like they strive to be the best of the best even more than Mnemon.<br /> <br /> As I\u2019m still not entirely sure what I want to do with my life, I find the idea of being tested at age 5 and then told \u201cyou\u2019re going to be doing this for the next 200 years\u201d deeply disconcerting. <br /> <br /> I find myself wondering if any dynast is actually happy.<br /> <br /> Not in debt to Ragara and still getting richer. Very nice. I wonder if they\u2019ve considered offering loans to the other houses yet? If they could free, say, Mnemon from Ragara\u2019s influence that might make them a powerful ally. Though, I suppose Mnemon might just take it as an insult. I have to imagine that there are some houses that would appreciate it though.<br /> <br /> Hmm... Nellens are the ants. Looked down upon, ignored, omnipresent, and, if they decide to march, very dangerous.<br /> <br /> I think my Eclipse Merchant would like these people and they would find her insights into Knowing the Prices of Souls likewise very useful. Pity that working with an Anathema would get their house torn up.<br /> <br /> \u201cOh, you\u2019re going to give me this skilled Dragon-Blooded commander just because she wasn\u2019t born here? Well, if you insist....\u201d<br /> <br /> If they\u2019re grabbing disgraced officers, I hope they\u2019re doing background checks first.<br /> <br /> This is a house that loves a bargain, but has a chip on its shoulder.<br /> <br /> The Empress kept sowing discord everywhere, just to make sure no-one could build alliances against her and so that everyone would be too busy playing her game instead of trying to build their own. Which worked ok while she was around, but now those birds that come home to roost have been revealed as circling vultures, just waiting for the place to collapse.<br /> <br /> I wonder if anyone in setting has figured out why all the infighting exists and that putting another Empress on the throne, even one that everyone liked, is only going to exacerbate the problem. Especially if the new Empress doesn\u2019t have the Sword of Creation to back up her authority.<br /> <br /> I honestly think that, at this point in the Realm\u2019s history, the Deliberative is going to need to step up and become an actual governing body, or the Realm will collapse entirely into infighting and each new Empress will have a lifespan of weeks at best after she takes the crown.<br /> <br /> Anyway.<br /> <br /> I hope they can find a way to work with V\u2019Neef because the two houses together might be able to destabilize the Ragara stranglehold on the Realm\u2019s financial systems.<br /> <br /> I could see a Nellens/Tepet alliance working very well.<br /> <br /> And having the unexalted masses behind them is a very nice bit of support.<br /> <br /> Do not dismiss the Nellens white weenie deck.<br /> <br /> I wonder if anyone tries to walk through all seven doorways once or whether they\u2019ve developed graph theory to prove that you can\u2019t.<br /> <br /> Juche sounds nice. And very profitable for the House.<br /> <br /> Supporting other satrapies sounds like it\u2019s been paying off nicely too.<br /> <br /> Nellens sounds interesting.<br /> <br /> I hope Sabine can pull it off. Good luck!<br /> <br /> ....There\u2019s a part of me that thinks that, if she succeeds, that\u2019s probably worthy of a Solar Exaltation...which is kinda horrible under those circumstances.<br /> <br /> I also can\u2019t help but think that finding a way to ally with Ledaal might be the key to this research.<br /> <br /> Like I said, my Eclipse merchant wishes she was this awesome.<br /> <br /> You go Uliya! Bureau of Standards represent!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-01T18:34:47-07:00","id":1202087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200185-brilliantrain-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1202071#post1202071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As I\u2019m still not entirely sure what I want to do with my life, I find the idea of being tested at age 5 and then told \u201cyou\u2019re going to be doing this for the next 200 years\u201d deeply disconcerting.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI think of it as being a support and assessment system that is able to effectively find your aptitudes and provide you with the means of cultivating and applying them. Dynasts aren't exactly struggling with the prospect of unemployment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find myself wondering if any dynast is actually happy.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bNellens Laferin seemed to be. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-01T18:58:11-07:00","id":1202097,"title":"","content":"Do you have a favourite character so far?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-01T23:08:08-07:00","id":1202143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200185-brilliantrain-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1202097#post1202097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you have a favourite character so far?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm... If I had to choose, probably Nellens Sabine, unluckiest potential Solar ever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-01T23:08:41-07:00","id":1202144,"title":"","content":"House Peleps <br /> <br /> Ok, so what did they do to you to make me like you?<br /> <br /> ...This is different.<br /> <br /> Dashing and adventurous. Pure and incorruptible. <br /> <br /> This is very different.<br /> <br /> Not bad though.<br /> <br /> Ah, Abbot and Costello and nautical humor.<br /> <br /> So they\u2019re a combination of the Lion and Unicorn clans then? The ones who went off to exotic foreign lands and are incorruptible and honorable.<br /> <br /> Ah-ha!<br /> <br /> ...oh, no, ok, I\u2019m actually kinda down with having to demonstrate some degree of worthiness for your position.<br /> <br /> So, you have to be lucky and awesome to make it in this house.<br /> <br /> So they\u2019re actually less honorable than they appear it sounds like. I am SHOCKED. SHOCKED I tell you.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m assuming that Peleps Orimu is a pirate hunter and not a judge who is also a pirate, awesome as that might be.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, we\u2019re not having a vote so you get a say. We\u2019re having a vote to prove which of us can manipulate the rest of you the best. <br /> <br /> They\u2019re debating between \u201ctry to rule the Realm OR fuck off and go take over the West and rule in an island paradise. Hmmmmm.....\u201d<br /> <br /> If you\u2019re not going to include a timeline in this book, you might wanna insert a reminder somewhere in the text of what the current year is, just to give us a reference for all the dates you keep throwing at us. Maybe in the Lexicon where you talk about the realm year you could say \u201cIt is currently RY whatever.\u201d<br /> <br /> Ok, so. Having one House oversee the entire navy on an island nation seems really dangerous. I\u2019m honestly surprised that the Empress let Peleps hold on to that monopoly for as long as she did. <br /> <br /> That said, if the Empress had stayed, I bet she\u2019d have done something like suggest to V\u2019Neef that they trade back some of the merchant marine for one of the navies or something. Unless she was planning to destroy Peleps and divide up the navy between a bunch of other houses.<br /> <br /> I have to say that squeezing your own Satrapies dry because you can always steal more does not sound virtuous.<br /> <br /> All of these methods sound very desperate.<br /> <br /> ....You\u2019re planning on creating an empire that\u2019s true to the Immaculate Order with all sorts of shady dealings?<br /> <br /> So, they\u2019re quietly sending an entire legion west, ready to take it over.<br /> <br /> So, if you do well and you\u2019re a DB woman, you can go fast....and fall hard if you\u2019ve got the least bit of scandal. That sounds like a fun character background. Once the rising star of the Peleps armada, then something happened, and now you\u2019re piloting a tug boat or garbage scow or something else humiliating. But it happens to be the only boat in the area when the other PCs show up and need a boat, and game progresses.<br /> <br /> Yeah, I really wonder what else would have happened to Peleps if the Empress has remained, because allowing one house to become powerful enough to possibly win a fight against most of the other houses seems like something she\u2019d have wanted to avoid.<br /> <br /> This reputation sounds more manufactured than real honestly.<br /> <br /> With all its debt, it seems odd not to explore its relations with Ragara in more depth than just \u201coh, yeah, it owes Ragara too, just like everyone else.\u201d<br /> <br /> Still a pretty cold blooded house.<br /> <br /> Interesting relationship with Cathak. The knowledge that the two of them could rule the world is interesting. A Cathak-Peleps-Mnemon alliance could force the war hot and make a few other houses, like Ledaal, join them and force the newer and/or disliked houses to band together against them. I really don\u2019t fancy the chances of V\u2019Neef, Tepet, Nellens, Sesus, or Ragara in that situation. Though, I could be wrong.<br /> <br /> That puts the military on one side and the economy and ninjas on the other. Which would be an interesting conflict.<br /> <br /> I want a book about the War in the West now. V\u2019Neef vs. Peleps in a region where neither of them has a complete stranglehold on everything, and there are plenty of non-Realm wild cards, will be interesting.<br /> <br /> Welp. Sarkarn is in a scylla and charybdis situation.<br /> <br /> Really, really want the War in the West now. Wavecrest sounds lots more interesting now than it did when the main thing you had to worry about was being arrested for jaywalking and having the sentence be \u201ctoss you into the volcano.\u201d<br /> <br /> Well you know what they say. If our ancestors were alive today, they\u2019d say \u201cwhy is it so dark in here? Where\u2019s the door?\u201d<br /> <br /> And here we come to one of the big reasons the War hasn\u2019t gone hot yet. Everyone in charge is still half way convinced that the Empress is going to show up tomorrow and do a massive re-org based on how everyone acted during the 5 years she was gone. And most of the Houses will have lots of explaining to do then.<br /> <br /> Aramida... wasn\u2019t she from one of the Aspect books?<br /> <br /> Good luck with that, Zurin. I hope you live through the attempt.<br /> <br /> Interesting house. Seems like its reputation as virtuous and adventurous is about as accurate as the Cynis one of drunken debouching is. In that they\u2019re both true to an extent, but they\u2019re also as much camouflage as anything else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-01T23:09:52-07:00","id":1202145,"title":"","content":"Two houses now, lest I not finish before the next section drops.<br /> <br /> House Ragara<br /> <br /> Ok, the book has made me hella curious here.<br /> <br /> So they\u2019re the \u201cgreed is good\u201d house?<br /> <br /> I hope there\u2019s a sidebar or something on how to play a \u201cgood\u201d Ragara.<br /> <br /> I find it very ironic that both Ragara and Ledaal are experimenting with sorcerous and blasphemous methods of enhancing Dragon Blooded, arguably for the same reasons.<br /> <br /> Ok, so, a large chunk of the house thinks they\u2019re \u201cjust\u201d cutthroat business people and investment bankers. Might still need that sidebar.<br /> <br /> Ah! Here\u2019s the connection between money, archaeology, and mysticism I was looking for.<br /> <br /> I feel like defaulting on your loans should be discussed somewhere. It\u2019s the nuclear option, yes, but if all of the other houses decided that they weren\u2019t gonna pay Ragara back, what would happen? I suppose they don\u2019t worry about it because trying to get all the houses together on one thing is like herding cats. And, as we saw with Tepet, you don\u2019t wanna be the only one who decides to just walk away from their debts, because the other houses will see that as a sign of weakness and eat you alive.<br /> <br /> That might be why they have the whole hidden blasphemy thing. If you can uncover that and expose it to the world, then Ragara as a house dies and everyone\u2019s debts are forgiven. Which is going to majorly change the power dynamics of the Realm.<br /> <br /> Sounds like Ragara did the same thing as Nellens and, while the Ragara legions are now better equipped, I suspect the Nellens legions are better staffed.<br /> <br /> If I ran a DB game, I think I might start it with a Ledaal exposing Ragara\u2019s blasphemous secrets on the Deliberative floor, just to kick off the war.<br /> <br /> A Sesus-Ragara-Cynis alliance would be interesting.<br /> <br /> Hmmm... I think I\u2019ll need to go back through all these, maybe make a graph of potential alliances. It would make for very interesting reading.<br /> <br /> Jau Dei, a secret cavern hiding blasphemous experimentation sounds a bit like an Avatar reference.<br /> <br /> I definitely need a sidebar on the politics and acceptability of assassination in the Realm, because I would have thought the Empress would\u2019ve had Ragara killed for that or something.<br /> <br /> Ok, so that\u2019s what Blood Zenith is. Interesting. I kinda wonder why he didn\u2019t go out and slay another Anathema or something.<br /> <br /> And Banoba\u2019s not so secret weakness and two scions who help the house out but would probably be horrified at what\u2019s actually going on to round things out.<br /> <br /> Oh and a Sidereal.<br /> <br /> Very interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T11:21:02-07:00","id":1202268,"title":"","content":"Ok another house.<br /> <br /> House Sesus<br /> <br /> Scorpion Clan Represent!<br /> <br /> Ok, did NOT expect to see house Sesus extolling the virtues of knowledge as the only important thing worth having.<br /> <br /> This is a very unusual interpretation of Hesiah\u2019s teachings.<br /> <br /> ......<br /> <br /> ......I dunno, maybe she should have let Ragara kill this one.<br /> <br /> So, like many other houses, this one is two houses in one. The outer house, full of everyone considered useless, and the inner one where the real power is.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s interesting to compare them to Cathak, who have a reputation as being dashing soldiers. While the Sesus socialites are even more charming for rising above their thuggish house.<br /> <br /> Ok, the masked council is cool, sure, but I can\u2019t help but imagine the stories involved in someone who isn\u2019t supposed to be there getting their hands on the mask and whatever passwords they need to get in. Like the child of one of the elders finding the secret door to the spy room with all the records and the mask and then trying to pass themselves off as the new Dread Pirate Roberts or something.<br /> <br /> Hmm... they also do some profiteering from conquered new Satrapies, just like Cathak. Interesting. So house Cathak builds a business as it\u2019s conquering a place, then flips the business to a Sesus cutout, who then sells it to Nellens at a profit. While Nellens turns it into a very nice going concern.<br /> <br /> Ok, so they have seven legions, which sounds like they have the second biggest army in the Realm (Peleps has a huge navy, not a huge army). I\u2019m not gonna say they could take Cathak, but Sesus would do everything they could to make sure that wasn\u2019t a fair fight and I am sure that they\u2019re better at trickery than Cathak.<br /> <br /> It really is sad that professional spies tend to have trust issues. House Cynis and House Sesus have so much to offer each other that merging their ninja squads would make them amazingly powerful.<br /> <br /> Wait, they were enemies with Tepet? Why? I thought they hated Nellens.<br /> <br /> Everything else makes sense.<br /> <br /> ....I feel like allowing Sesus to maintain a prison is asking for trouble.<br /> <br /> Silken Diamond, mountaintop resort/ninja training center.<br /> <br /> Isle of Smoke sounds cool. Really all the locations have been awesome.<br /> <br /> I kinda feel like maybe there should have been a Tepet Satrapy in the Ragara section too, given that they also did that sort of thing.<br /> <br /> This makes me wanna read Tepet though.<br /> <br /> For the record, I bet she\u2019s actually buried somewhere completely different. I mean, if I was a master manipulator who liked mind games, I\u2019d have my secret tomb built and hidden by various means.... then arrange for my actual body to be taken away by mortals and buried somewhere, with a decent ceremony, but without any marks or anything. And I\u2019d make sure I was buried with an important artifact.<br /> <br /> See if you can find that, you young bastards.<br /> <br /> .....ok, I did not see that coming. The dirty tricks house is run by a Matriarch who refuses to use her ninjas. Weird. Well that\u2019s shooting herself in the foot.<br /> <br /> Married to a son of the Empress....doesn\u2019t that mean she married her uncle?<br /> <br /> That might actually deserve a sidebar somewhere too, possibly titled \u201cSo your family tree doesn\u2019t branch.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cLady Smoke? I don\u2019t believe she exists.\u201d<br /> <br /> More seriously, I could buy her as a house legend that enough people have used for their own purposes that everyone thinks she actually exists now. To the point that she\u2019s become the \u201ctenth\u201d member of the Masked Council and they collectively determine what she\u2019s been up to at every meeting, dropping just enough evidence that she actually exists to make people buy into it.<br /> <br /> Well, or she\u2019s actually a Lunar. (Because I have trouble imagining that DB Stealth and Larceny are so much more powerful than DB Awareness and Investigation and Lunars are naturally adept at trickery, that\u2019s why).<br /> <br /> That actually might merit a sidebar too. How do they keep Lunars from sneaking in as rats on ships and then listening in corners and following people until they know enough secrets to ruin some people and who to deliver that info to and then watching the carnage?<br /> <br /> I really do like Sesus Rafara. I assume that, at the very least, the thing about her being given extra special training to turn her into the ultimate spy, without asking her opinion on the matter and basically ruining her future, is still accurate.<br /> <br /> Ok, I want Terel to miscalculate badly at some point now.<br /> <br /> Interesting new take on the old house of thugs and jerks. Possibly some more explicit notes on what the house looks like to everyone else would be nice, but I can run with it as is. Given that other houses are noted as being annoyed at having to root out Sesus spies, I don\u2019t think their whole secret ninja thing is as well kept a secret as they think, so the section might want to be rewritten a bit to make that a little less implied.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T11:42:09-07:00","id":1202274,"title":"","content":"On the subject of the virtues of House Peleps, I'm reminded of when people would comment on the HBO Rome show in terms of drinking a shot whenever Lucius Vorenus acted like a good Roman and a terrible person.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T11:57:29-07:00","id":1202277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200185-brilliantrain-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1202274#post1202274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the subject of the virtues of House Peleps, I'm reminded of when people would comment on the HBO Rome show in terms of drinking a shot whenever Lucius Vorenus acted like a good Roman and a terrible person.</div> </div> </div> </div>You'd die of alcohol poisoning int he first few episodes, but not a bad analogy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T16:55:19-07:00","id":1202342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200185-brilliantrain-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1202274#post1202274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the subject of the virtues of House Peleps, I'm reminded of when people would comment on the HBO Rome show in terms of drinking a shot whenever Lucius Vorenus acted like a good Roman and a terrible person.</div> </div> </div> </div>There\u2019s enough overlap between the Immaculate Philosophy and what we think of as virtuous behavior that I still feel like I can call them out on it. That may change after we get a better look at it, I dunno.<br /> <br /> I will grant that backroom dealings, underhanded political maneuvering, and stabbing people in the back are typical behaviors of the Scarlet Dynasty, so exemplars of it shouldn\u2019t shy away from such things. But I still can\u2019t call such things virtuous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T16:55:50-07:00","id":1202343,"title":"","content":"Anyway, Tepet time!<br /> <br /> House Tepet<br /> <br /> I read the preview, but I wanna read this one again.<br /> <br /> Very nice intro section, very evocative and very good at introducing the central conflict of the house.<br /> <br /> Tepet, adversary turned ally turned lover.<br /> <br /> And, with their failure, no-one wants to be associated with the unlucky house, especially when they have incentive to tear it up and steal anything they have left.<br /> <br /> They face this doom as warriors.<br /> <br /> The Sublime Armigers and Yamabushi sound interesting. Are there any other mechanics we need that we don\u2019t already have? Knowing more about the philosophy would be nice too, certainly, but mechanics are tricky.<br /> <br /> I love the bits of heroic worldbuilding in their background.<br /> <br /> This write up really drives home just how much their downfall was orchestrated by the other houses as it was from their military failure. It also serves as a very nice example of what awaits any of the other houses who move too soon, expose the wrong secret, or otherwise show too much weakness.<br /> <br /> Well, I assume Iselsi will too, but I\u2019m not there yet. And Tepet has lost pretty much everything in three years, but still has a ghost of a chance at building itself back up, so it\u2019s a good recent example of what can happen as well as showing us how you can maybe recover. While Iselsi was destroyed many more years ago, with the remnants biding their time, rebuilding their power, and waiting for the best time to strike, so they\u2019re an example of what a long lost house might still be able to do.<br /> <br /> Oh, that\u2019s a good note. \u201cOh, we\u2019ll grab these Satrapies that Tepet used to administer, the ones where they trained the locals in combat, and we\u2019ll treat them like our own personal banks, because obviously the Tepet broke their spirit for us, so it\u2019ll be fine.\u201d Yeah, keep telling yourself that dude.<br /> <br /> How many times do we need to tell you, Diversify your portfolio!<br /> <br /> The warrior\u2019s code aspect is really cool. Though, I confess, I\u2019m curious how they\u2019d react to someone who claimed an entirely unvirtuous code? Like one that said \u201cNever give a sucker an even break\u201d was their code. Would they accept that (and maybe sell you off to Sesus and forget about you) or would they tell you to pick another one?<br /> <br /> I suspect there\u2019s a lot of pressure during your formative years to pick an honorable and virtuous code and a lot of questions and \u201cencouragement\u201d to pick a code the house finds acceptable when it comes time to formally choose. And, if a scion chooses poorly, they probably have places they send washouts and stuff, but I suspect that, while they might not approve of your choice, they\u2019ll still respect that you made the choice and, if you do live by that code, you might get some grudging respect for it.<br /> <br /> I had a player who had a Tepet character in a game I ran. I\u2019ll need to ask what the character\u2019s code would have been.<br /> <br /> So, they\u2019ve got a legion and a half, mostly lacking officers and full of criminals and drunks. I think Cathak had the right of it. <br /> <br /> Ok, it sounds like House Sesus is actually in the process of walking away from its debts already. Should be interesting how this plays out for them.<br /> <br /> That said, I still wanna know what the beef is between Sesus and Tepet.<br /> <br /> I really like the idea of a Tepet-V\u2019Neef-Nellens coalition. I think it could be a surprisingly powerful block. Especially with some Iselsi backing.<br /> <br /> It always saddens me when the \u201chonorable warriors\u201d stab each other in the back.<br /> <br /> Granted, actual combat has few rules, other than \u201cwin\u201d and \u201cmake sure you can pay the cost of winning.\u201d So I kind of question the actual existence and effectiveness of the \u201chonorable warrior\u201d to begin with too.<br /> <br /> Taking over Ithen would be an interesting challenge.<br /> <br /> Tepet Niruz is very cool. All the other Tepts are awesome too.<br /> <br /> Very, very good writeup.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T20:19:44-07:00","id":1202415,"title":"","content":"House V'Neef<br /> <br /> Full disclosure. This house is likely to play an important role in my current game, so I've been very curious about it. I also rather like it.<br /> <br /> Ok, nice beginning. Sets up the conflict of the house and says what they're doing to deal with it.<br /> <br /> Bending like the willow is a very apt metaphor<br /> <br /> This house may be a young sapling, but it's growing with the vigor of youth and boldly sending runners out whichever way it can, because a storm's a coming.<br /> <br /> Popular, you're gonna be popular.<br /> <br /> Sounds like she's pretty sure that, if she's not on the throne in five year's time, she and her entire family will be dead in a ditch somewhere<br /> <br /> It's funny. Given that the tribute is drying up and what is coming back is likely being escorted by whatever troops and ships that house can scrounge up, instead of the Merchant fleet and/or their income is being under reported and so on, because who wants to pay V'Neef if they can keep it for themselves, it sounds like Peleps would be bleeding even MORE money if they still had to worry about the Merchant Fleet.<br /> <br /> (admittedly, they'd have had lots more money to begin with if they hadn't lost it years ago, but...)<br /> <br /> Really want a War in the West book.<br /> <br /> Ok, so they have one legion on defense with lots of excellent leadership, one legion to deploy as needed, and they're not gonna spook anyone by sending their ships wherever they want. Sounds ....adequate. I can't help but think that allying with Nellens and Tepet the three of them could probably field a fighting force that could be reckoned with.<br /> Or at least not just swept aside out of hand.<br /> <br /> ........That saddens me. Even V'Neef betrays Tepet now. I expected better from you. ;_;<br /> <br /> Ah, economic warfare from Ragara. Expected.<br /> <br /> Time for the elephant in the room. It's funny. What V'Neef fears from Mnemon is exactly what I would have expected from her before. But, after reading her entry....I don't think she'd crush House V'Neef out of spite or petty jealousy. If V'Neef, say, went to Mnemon and offered to support her bid for the throne and was honest and supportive about it, I think Mnemon would accept it.<br /> <br /> This is yet another case where Mnemon preferring to be feared works against her.<br /> <br /> .....That said, I am now imagining V'Neef giving Mnemon a makeover while singing Popular, from Wicked.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OkZpq4DFimk\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OkZpq4DFimk\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OkZpq4DFimk </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OkZpq4DFimk\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OkZpq4DFimk </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I hope they discuss the relationship with Nellens.<br /> <br /> Heh. And V'Neef provides a rallying flag for anyone who hates/fears Peleps and/or Mnemon.<br /> <br /> Well, if they do drop her, she'll have pretty much nothing left to lose, so my V'Neef-Nellens-Tepet ship could sail, but only after V'Neef gets desperate enough.<br /> <br /> Oooh. Helping out the Magistrates, nice move.<br /> <br /> Eagle's Launch sounds like a wonderful place to set a game in and a terrible place to live (right now).<br /> I like Seven Cardinals already.<br /> <br /> Everyone is fortifying everything and cutting whatever deals they need to, in order to stay alive.<br /> <br /> Chejop, you really should have seen this coming. If not this, then something like it happening if the Empress ever died suddenly. You should have had a contingency ready, even if it was as lame as wearing a dress and pretending to be her.<br /> <br /> REALLY, REALLY, REALLY want War in the West.<br /> <br /> !<br /> Is the Caul a V'Neef holding?!?<br /> ok, sounds like no, they just have a major garrison there that sounds like a cross between the Winchester Mystery House and a paranoid Dungeon Master's Zombie Bunker.<br /> I've been told that Faxai is V'Neef's...which basically means the entire Caul is technically hers, except for the minor Anathema problem.<br /> <br /> I hope they decide to run the section on the Caul as a preview during the KS<br /> <br /> V'Neef sounds like she'd be a fairly capable leader, but I doubt anyone could actually handle being the new Empress. Without the Sword of Creation and the status granted from literally being everyone's mother and the perception that she's always been there and always will, I don't think anyone could govern this nest of vipers for any real length of time.<br /> <br /> They're either gonna need to finally learn from the mistakes of the Shogunate and come together and actually turn the deliberative into a governing body... or the Realm will turn into a collection of petty kingdoms, fighting over land and resources.<br /> <br /> .......I kinda wanna make a Solar who sneaks into the Imperial Manse and manages to take control of it and then uses disguise charms and the giant illusion thing it can do to stage the Return of the Empress, call all the houses out on their selfishness and idiocy, and formally put the Deliberative in charge. That would be such a bad idea in so many ways I can't even count them, but I get so annoyed at the fact that everyone has locked themselves into thinking that there has to be an Empress.<br /> <br /> Anyway<br /> <br /> S'thera sounds like a villain name, but I feel sympathy for her plight.<br /> .....I'm also curious what Tepet Kedus's gender was. There don't seem to be any general indications that a dynastic name is feminine or masculine.<br /> <br /> That said, I'll grant that, if V'Neef really thinks she has a shot at wooing Cathak to her camp, allying with Tepet too heavily right now could be a problem. One of her major assets is marriageable overbred sons and practically giving them to Tepet isn't really going to help either house.<br /> <br /> Dancing Boar is also sympathetic.<br /> <br /> *sigh* Well, it's like they say, if the demons don't get you, the moneylenders will. I bet the blueprints have deliberate errors in them too.<br /> <br /> I like them. A young house in a dangerous position, but they've managed to stay afloat for now.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T20:29:55-07:00","id":1202418,"title":"","content":"As an aside, I'm currently taking a class in graph theory and one of the things we've been discussing is graphs of friends and enemies and how to see how things break up into camps. I might try and post a very simplified graph of the House relationships and see if there are any obvious fracture patterns.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T21:00:34-07:00","id":1202433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200185-brilliantrain-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1202277#post1202277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You'd die of alcohol poisoning int he first few episodes, but not a bad analogy.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Off topic for a sec, but other great Rome drinking games included<br /> <br /> - taking a shot every times the news caller completely reversed his political position (I told Ian McNeice about that one at a con)<br /> <br /> Or using this wonderful chart...<br /> <br /> A Sip: Octavian outsmarts somebody.<br /> <br /> Two sips: Posca outsmarts somebody.<br /> <br /> Three sips: Atia outsmarts somebody. <br /> <br /> Four sips: Antony outsmarts somebody. <br /> <br /> Finish your glass: Pullo outsmarts somebody.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T21:58:26-07:00","id":1202445,"title":"","content":"I'm assuming Pullo is the dumb one? (I don't watch Rome.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T22:08:16-07:00","id":1202447,"title":"","content":"Iselsi<br /> <br /> Well that got dark quickly. Only to be expected, sure, but....<br /> <br /> &quot;There is no House Iselsi. There is only its hungry ghost.&quot; That gave me chills and really sums up everything you need to know about them. Kudos to the author.<br /> Really, everyone who worked on this has just done an amazing job.<br /> <br /> The death masks with their deeds carved into them is wonderfully spooky.<br /> <br /> I have to wonder what made their leadership think they could actually assassinate the Scarlet Empress.<br /> <br /> The mental gymnastics required of being Iselsi make me wonder if the DBs have persona charms.<br /> <br /> It also makes me think of Umineko<br /> <br /> .....The Empress really has a lot to answer for.<br /> That said.....based on the Shogunate.... Well, I could imagine someone saying &quot;If there is to be perpetual infighting, I shall build a system where the infighting is bent towards breaking itself. Thus, shall the house stand strong.&quot; or some other such poetic nonsense.<br /> <br /> Building a single point of failure into your structure may have doomed the world.<br /> <br /> See! I bet the Lady of Smoke is just like them.<br /> <br /> Man, this sort of terrorist cell structure is hella difficult to root out.<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh, you only have enough money to send your kids to a second tier college and buy a small yacht. Poor you, how you must suffer.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm curious what Mnemon has against them this time around. Sesus I can buy being dicks for the hell of it.<br /> <br /> Whenever the elders give the go order, it'll make the Red Wedding look like a children's party.<br /> <br /> Ok, it sounds like several patrician families, Nellens, Ragara, and now Iselsi are the ones who are up in the Thousand Scales<br /> <br /> Ok, so Sesus wants their rival ninja clan gone and Mnemon wants the traitorous scum out of the priesthood. Ok, makes sense.<br /> <br /> So, they maybe hate V'Neef less than the others, but not much.<br /> <br /> Huh. Ok, not surprised by the offer from Nellens. That.....actually could be useful. Hmmm....<br /> The Tepet option was also mentioned. Which....hmmm....<br /> It's weird, things are actually aligning fairly well for this group of DB NPCs in my game to make a decent degree of sense.<br /> <br /> &quot;psst. Hey you. Yeah, you, the god of divine judgement. How'd you like another day in the local immaculate calendar and to get in on the ground floor of the biggest righteous revenge attempt since we killed the Solar Anathema?&quot;<br /> <br /> The House of Black Waters is very appropriate.<br /> <br /> ....I can't help but think of Major Kira from DS9, so I guess Kiera gets to be played by Nana Visitor if she ever comes up.<br /> I'll admit that I too speculate on how she got their trust.<br /> <br /> A Classic Ninja village rendered as they probably actually were, not as fiction would have them be.<br /> <br /> I think I might have liked Iselsi. Somewhat anyway. I can respect a smart mathematician, but ruthlessness has never appealed to me. I do wonder what she would have thought about what her house has become. I bet she would have murdered the ones who tried and failed to assassinate the Empress herself though.<br /> <br /> I bet many in your house feel the same way Dileko.<br /> <br /> For the record, I think that feuds and the cycle of violence are inherently stupid and they need to be stopped and rooted out wherever possible. In this particular case, that's going to be a lot harder than usual for these sorts of stories, because a good chunk of all of the original parties are still around, so you could, theoretically, get &quot;justice&quot; against the parties who wronged you without having to take out the entire Realm as collateral damage.<br /> .......Full disclosure, I do have a weakness for the The Count of Monte Cristo and Leverage. I get revenge. I enjoy revenge. But.... there comes a point when there's no point to it. Do you really want to waste your talents going on one final killing spree, or do you actually want to make the world a better place? Help create something more worthwhile than a pile of corpses.<br /> <br /> Anyway.<br /> <br /> See? Moonless River gets it. She'll be making the Realm a much better place by her actions.<br /> <br /> Ok, raise your hand if you think that Iselsi Takora is actually a Lunar.<br /> <br /> I think I need more context to fully understand Iselsi Shenesh","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T22:11:52-07:00","id":1202448,"title":"","content":"I'm still confused about why Sesus hates Tepet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-02T22:21:37-07:00","id":1202454,"title":"","content":"Ok, this cadet houses section explains a lot, thank you and introduces some cool new options.<br /> <br /> And with that, I'm done, narrowly before the next chunk drops.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T03:49:59-07:00","id":1202517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200185-brilliantrain-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1202448#post1202448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm still confused about why Sesus hates Tepet.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI think that all the military Houses had a certain rivalry, but Cathak being what it was, they were less acrimonious about it.<br /> <br /> \u200bIt might not be stated in the book, but I can also imagine that many Sesus would dislike Tepet's business of training states in the Threshold to be able to fight for themselves, as that undercut their mercenary business.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T04:31:30-07:00","id":1202523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200185-brilliantrain-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1202448#post1202448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm still confused about why Sesus hates Tepet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Reading between the lines, petty envy. House Sesus had been entrusted with the larger potion of the Realm's military strength, but <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">House </span></span></span>Tepet had still earned the greater reputation and respect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":487,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","user":"Greyman","date":".  Why does this textbox put random linebreaks in the text? 04-03-2018, 07:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T05:20:19-07:00","id":1202526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200185-brilliantrain-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1202523#post1202523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">House Sesus had been entrusted with the larger potion of the Realm's military strength</div> </div> </div> </div>How do you figure?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T13:47:10-07:00","id":1202716,"title":"","content":"Ok, chunk two!<br /> <br /> As I read DBWFHW, part 2<br /> <br /> Chapter fiction<br /> <br /> dynast from our sworn kinship is dissatisfied with marriage and life.<br /> <br /> I wondered if they were happy.<br /> <br /> Interesting lead in.<br /> <br /> This explains so much.<br /> <br /> I suppose it\u2019s easier to view your child as a resource when you don\u2019t know them very well. It also lessens the pain if they don\u2019t exalt, I imagine.<br /> <br /> I am glad they have some source of empathy growing up.<br /> <br /> Repeated a sentence.<br /> <br /> Right, because most of them are going five or ten years between children. So ver little chance for siblings. <br /> <br /> What are leftover children?<br /> <br /> Note on orphans and same sex couples. Apparently there are species of animals that produce gay couples too and they adopt orphans as well.<br /> <br /> Will the Realm discuss patrician and peasant life?<br /> <br /> I think it\u2019s worth noting that when someone expects to get something, they start to feel like they already own it. If they don\u2019t receive what they expected, they feel like it\u2019s been taken away. This seems like an important thing to remember going forward about Dynastic life.<br /> <br /> Ok so that\u2019s why those schools, got it.<br /> <br /> Good info on differences in basic education.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/WickedCultured\" target=\"_blank\">http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.ph...WickedCultured</a><br /> <br /> I have a rambunctious nephew which gives me an interesting perspective on just how difficult it must be to get most of these children to behave like that.<br /> <br /> The home schooling sidebar was basically written for Sesus Rafara. Part of the reason she\u2019s mad is because she was home schooled to be the perfect ninja and taught as much as possible to have an outsider\u2019s perspective on the Realm, to the point that they basically turned her into an outcaste, ensured that she would marry poorly, and really just not get any of the benefits that any other DB Dynast gets. In the process, their teaching methods invalidated the standard indoctrination methods they use to promote loyalty to your house without them realizing it.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m glad they left in the exaltation rituals and things that children practice. It\u2019s really only to be expected.<br /> <br /> The paragraph that starts \u201cThere are hundreds of primary schools located around the Blessed Isle, plus a few of lesser quality in satrapies with sizable Dynastic populations or cadet houses\u201d feels like it was meant to introduce this section so it\u2019s a little weird to see it all the way down here.<br /> <br /> And now I want a character for whom school was a significant upgrade in terms of lifestyle.<br /> <br /> They haven\u2019t changed the curriculum in hundreds of years? Interesting. Makes sense for their purposes, I suppose.<br /> <br /> Specialization seems logical.<br /> <br /> So they\u2019re basically studying from the moment they wake up until their head hits the pillow at night. That\u2019s intense. Of course the environment is intensely competitive.<br /> <br /> And a note about the Reform schools closes out the Primary schools section. Though, I think Arada turned out ok. <br /> <br /> Good info, good section.<br /> <br /> Next, Secondary schools.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T19:54:32-07:00","id":1202850,"title":"","content":"Isn't Rafara's backstory different now, in keeping with the general theme of the House? Didn't she attend the same spy school situated in a spa that the rest of the Sesus did? I don't think she was necessarily home-schooled.<br /> <br /> \u200b{Cue a developer or Lea coming in to clarify that she's among the ones that are home-schooled}","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T08:31:04-07:00","id":1203018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200185-brilliantrain-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1202850#post1202850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't Rafara's backstory different now, in keeping with the general theme of the House? Didn't she attend the same spy school situated in a spa that the rest of the Sesus did? I don't think she was necessarily home-schooled.<br /> <br /> \u200b{Cue a developer or Lea coming in to clarify that she's among the ones that are home-schooled}</div> </div> </div> </div>from what we've been given so far, I'd say it was unclear. I'm just laying out why she was bitter back in 1e and how it still makes sense in 3e. I have no idea if it has been officially changed or not.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T20:42:14-07:00","id":1203274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200185-brilliantrain-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1203018#post1203018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> from what we've been given so far, I'd say it was unclear. I'm just laying out why she was bitter back in 1e and how it still makes sense in 3e. I have no idea if it has been officially changed or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Her big thing is she had some pretty unique trauma with her nannies, which as the current manuscript notes actually are people DBs might get attached to, being pretty brutally murdered in front of her. Then she was raised away from society to make her purposefully isolated, an outsider, and generally lacking any real meaningful social connections, friends, or any of that. And she's now been through about a century of this.<br /> <br /> Basically in context of Sesus, she's kind of an extreme case and at some point a straw broke the camel's back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-04T22:12:34-07:00","id":1203300,"title":"","content":"Secondary School<br /> <br /> So, generally speaking, if a child has a preference for a particular school, that\u2019s really only taken into account as much as it\u2019ll make them more likely to excel or their talents align in that direction. But plenty of other reasons might influence their choice of schools.<br /> <br /> In this society it really is who you know.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://narbonic.com/comic/october-14-19-2002/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://s0.wp.com/i/blank.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://narbonic.com/comic/october-14-19-2002/\" target=\"_blank\"> Mell Expelled: October 14-19, 2002 </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://narbonic.com/comic/october-14-19-2002/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://narbonic.com/comic/october-14-19-2002/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Visit the post for more. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Important info about mortals. Good luck to anyone who tries.<br /> <br /> I wonder if anyone has ever tried to fake an Exaltation?<br /> <br /> Oooh! Alternatives to the big four. Nice! I\u2019ve been wondering about those.<br /> <br /> I wonder what someone would have to do to turn one of these \u201clesser schools\u201d into a rival to the big four. Probably not possible now that the Empress is gone, at least in the short term. You\u2019d need to find a way to get a large chunk of the current crop of DB students to go there, because the networking opportunities are half the reason they go to these schools. Pretty much the only way I think it could work is by convincing the Peleps Matriarch that you\u2019ll provide a better education for all the children of her house for free than they\u2019d get anywhere else, which is a feat even an Eclipse would find daunting, and then leverage that acceptance to convince several other House Matriarchs to \u201cdonate\u201d enough money to keep the school going while still \u201cdemanding\u201d less than half what the other schools do, while weathering the sabotage from all four of the other schools whose students you\u2019re poaching.<br /> <br /> Could be a fun game concept.<br /> <br /> Anyway.<br /> <br /> Cloister of Wisdom<br /> <br /> Do not compare it to catholic school.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou have come to me asking that I be your guide along the path of Ti Kwan Leep, but be warned. To learn its ways, you must learn the ways of your own soul. Let us meditate upon this wisdom now.\u201d<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/Z8VD4JXUozM\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/Z8VD4JXUozM\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/Z8VD4JXUozM\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/Z8VD4JXUozM </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> ....I joke, but I could actually see that sketch being played out on the first day of classes here with some of the new students wanting to learn how to invert someone\u2019s digestive tract or punch people\u2019s souls off or whatever other nifty move they heard about.<br /> <br /> See! The book agrees with me!<br /> <br /> Ok, they have their own informants and ninjas too. It\u2019s only to be expected I suppose.<br /> <br /> Hmm! That was shorter than I expected, but fairly informative.<br /> <br /> Heptagram<br /> <br /> Good point about sorcery.<br /> <br /> I think it was 60 in previous editions, but a few dozen works. Thinking on it, maybe 77 should be the class size, just to continue with the theme.<br /> <br /> So, it\u2019s likely that you\u2019ll have one on one time with a tutor and \u201cclasses\u201d might be more like you and a lab partner doing hands on research under a sorcerer\u2019s supervision. That sounds pretty nice, honestly.<br /> <br /> I can\u2019t help but think of the Naming class from the Wise Man\u2019s Fear.<br /> <br /> I wonder if anyone attends the school for a grounding in occult adjacent studies, like Alchemy, Geomancy, and Artificing without trying to become a Sorcerer?<br /> <br /> Nice sidebar on sorcery. I wonder how much work it would take to become a popular sorcerer? I\u2019d imagine you\u2019d have to cultivate an air of ...well, whatever the opposite of what people think sorcery is and do it so hard that, if anyone hears that you went to the Heptagram, they assume you flunked out after a year. No demon or elemental bodyguards or other weird stuff. Like at all. It honestly might be hard to have time to yourself without people wondering if you\u2019re brewing curses or something, if they\u2019ve heard.<br /> <br /> No, what you do is pretend you\u2019re not a sorcerer so hard and so convincingly that, if people find evidence to the contrary, they dismiss it or find an alternative explanation for it.<br /> <br /> Creating a character who finds sorcery interesting and is innately good at it, but doesn\u2019t want to pay the social cost to master it...and then gets sent to the Heptagram because the House said so, could be interesting.<br /> <br /> Heck, anyone who wanted to go to a different school than they did could be interesting.<br /> <br /> Thinking on it, a character who is just gleefully sorcerous could be fun too. The kind of person who rides a cloud everywhere, trades hair with her friends so they can share dreams, and basically just treats sorcery like this matter of fact thing. Would probably get shuffled off somewhere they won\u2019t embarrass their house though. Or maybe a permanent position at the Heptagram.<br /> <br /> Speaking of, I want a book that goes into the Secondary Schools in detail. Yes, everyone likes the Heptagram, but I have faith that you guys can make the others cool too.<br /> <br /> Anyway<br /> <br /> House of Bells<br /> <br /> Why the House of Bells? I mean, I don\u2019t really think of Bells and Warfare at the same time.<br /> <br /> \u201cLeave us alone Mel Brooks!\u201d<br /> <br /> And now I\u2019m imagining one of the villages that\u2019s been assaulted by students so often, everyone living there has just gotten used to it, either heading for storm shelters or just ...walking around the fighting, maybe taking bets. Depends on how humorous you wanna play it. Also how much you wanna play up collateral damage.<br /> <br /> Glad to hear flunking out is more common than dying. Having your Fang graded together though.... That seems like it could promote \u201caccidents\u201d for those deemed truly hopeless by their peers.<br /> <br /> Oh wow. Promoting trained officers over those whose parents bribed everyone to get them into that position? What IS this world coming to.<br /> <br /> So, they\u2019re getting them used to managing on 4 hours sleep while doing the most strenuous tasks they can find. That\u2019s pretty grueling.<br /> <br /> I wonder just how many criminals ever make it.<br /> <br /> I like the squad names and things.<br /> <br /> <br /> Spiral Academy <br /> <br /> So, lets see if they made the boring academy cool.<br /> <br /> Good points as to its existence.<br /> <br /> They\u2019re not only teach these students, they\u2019re using the place like a giant economic computer.<br /> <br /> Naturally they\u2019re profiting off this six ways from Sunday.<br /> <br /> Good notes on teaching there.<br /> <br /> Ok, job prospects are useful.<br /> <br /> Oh? It\u2019s also the spy school. Nifty.<br /> <br /> Yeah, the secret school you can only attend when you find it is neat.<br /> <br /> Ok, I like it.<br /> <br /> And all kinds of secret societies too. <br /> <br /> A Spiral Academy game could be pretty fun with all kinds of social intrigue and manipulation.<br /> <br /> <br /> Paisap\u2019s Stair<br /> <br /> This school is hella hardcore. I guess one of the big differences between this place and the House of Bells, is that you can flunk out of the latter, while you can only die out of the former. And the \u201caccidents\u201d I was wondering about before all happen here.<br /> <br /> I bet House Nellens is cleaning up with these graduates.<br /> <br /> Sidebar on dropping out. Good to know you can make good. And the whole taking a year off after college thing is a very useful adventuring conceit. It makes sense, sure, but it also serves as a good way to have a group of starter level DBs without any real expectations on them and can end up wherever the hell they need to be for the game to work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":226,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","user":"BrilliantRain","date":". 04-05-2018, 01:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T03:12:11-07:00","id":1203350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200185-brilliantrain-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1203300#post1203300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder how much work it would take to become a popular sorcerer?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI feel as though Mnemon is close, at least by virtue of being a matriarch, but I also think that association with sorcery is part of why she's the way she is.<br /> <br /> \u200bRagara Szaya sounds like she's kind of well-liked, so I guess that an alternate path is to employ one's sorcery more adventurously, out in the Threshold; you get to bring back exotic benefits to the House, interesting stories, and you don't need to be around to freak people out a lot.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T15:31:12-07:00","id":1203544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200185-brilliantrain-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1203300#post1203300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> House of Bells<br /> <br /> Why the House of Bells? I mean, I don\u2019t really think of Bells and Warfare at the same time.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It's a reference to the sound of training when the weapons clang and bash off of shields and armour<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11701-fiikragg","name":"Fiikragg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11701_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T18:02:25-07:00","id":1203596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200185-brilliantrain-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1201412#post1201412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spider ridden Kubal? Sounds interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>What or where might that be? I have a Wood Aspect with a family connection to giant spiders for whom it could potentially be of interest/relevance, i guess...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T18:17:22-07:00","id":1203603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200185-brilliantrain-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1203596#post1203596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What or where might that be? I have a Wood Aspect with a family connection to giant spiders for whom it could potentially be of interest/relevance, i guess...<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s from the Cynis writeup where they discuss Greyfalls:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The satrapy of <b>Greyfalls</b> is the Realm\u2019s easternmost bastion in the Scavenger Lands, named for the tremendous waterfall that cascades down the cliff side. A recent Cynis acquisition, it\u2019s the site of one of the war manses that channels Creation\u2019s geomantic Essence into the Realm Defense Grid, and as such an invaluable strategic holding. It also serves as the Realm\u2019s gateway to Eastern trade with Ixcoatli, <b>spider-ridden Kubal</b>, the Jaguar Principalities, and other nations along the Golden Road trade route. It\u2019s a lucrative satrapy, but the sheer distance between it and the Blessed Isle poses a substantial obstacle to collecting tribute and maintaining control. As House Cynis prepares for the prospect of civil war, some within it wonder whether they\u2019d be best served by simply cutting Greyfalls loose, leaving its satrap to fend for herself. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":226,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","user":"BrilliantRain","date":". 04-05-2018, 11:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T18:52:09-07:00","id":1203619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200185-brilliantrain-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1203603#post1203603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It\u2019s from the Cynis writeup where they discuss Greyfalls:<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Short, vague but evocative. Now even more tempted to tinker with in relation to the Sinasi spider-riders of previous games. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-05T21:28:06-07:00","id":1203700,"title":"","content":"dragon-blooded are really gay, and i love love love it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1201-fitter-happier","name":"Fitter Happier","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1201_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T03:30:31-07:00","id":1203775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fitter Happier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200185-brilliantrain-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1203700#post1203700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">dragon-blooded are really gay, and i love love love it.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://media.giphy.com/media/kcy0ZbKN4Q4yQ/giphy.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T12:12:44-07:00","id":1204934,"title":"","content":"Looks like you got your wish. It's not a standalone book, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>At $221,000 in funding - HEIRS TO THE SHOGUNATE \u2013 REALM EXPANSION #1</b><span style=\"color:#282828\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">: War in the West \u2013 A section dealing with the impending war between House Peleps and House V\u2019neef will be added to the Dragon-Blooded Companion PDF.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8890-nullapostle","name":"NullApostle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T18:34:20-07:00","id":1205038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NullApostle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200185-brilliantrain-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1204934#post1204934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looks like you got your wish. It's not a standalone book, though.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yup. I\u2019m very excited.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T09:28:44-07:00","id":1205249,"title":"","content":"So, I ran out of time, read over the rest of Dynasic upbringing without taking notes, took a few notes on outcastes, and went back and made a few notes on Lookshy politics. So, I\u2019ll post what I\u2019ve got here presently and then move on to the new chunk.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not promising any notes on the charms. I\u2019m not even promising to read anything but Archery, Craft, and Dodge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T09:29:47-07:00","id":1205250,"title":"","content":"Lookshy<br /> <br /> Politics <br /> <br /> Ok, so generally speaking, I think the Isolationist faction and the Purist faction were both likely to see Lookshy become a Satrapy within a decade or two. Well, or a smoking crater. To keep out the Realm Dragon long term, you need a highly prepared military with plenty of their own DBs, something of similar power, or enough distance from the Realm that it\u2019s not worth it. Lookshy sits on the Realm\u2019s doorstep and their troves of First Age magic are dwindling by the day, so that military might is really the only thing that stops them becoming a cadet house at best. Shrinking the military and going into business with the Realm is pretty much saying \u201csure, we\u2019ll be glad to be a satrapy.\u201d Alternately, sending the military out to fight a bunch of wars to \u201cpurify the River Province\u201d is a good way to waste your military strength and alienate/destroy historical allies so that you won\u2019t be able to hold the Realm back the next time they show up.<br /> <br /> However.<br /> <br /> That was then. Now... I honestly can\u2019t say that inviting House Tepet to rejoin the Seventh Legion or whatever the Imperialists want is inherently a bad idea. And, once the Realm Civil War starts, between the fighting and aftermath they\u2019ll be unlikely to be able to field another major war for decades. So, temporarily diverting some military spending into the civilian budget for a few years to help grow your economy right now could pay off big time. Or, you could build up the military even more, preparing to strike at the Realm or \u201ccleanse\u201d the River Province at the right moment.<br /> <br /> All of those could be viable tactics at this point. It\u2019s not clear.<br /> <br /> (Arguably you could even try to find a couple of Solar Anathema Artificer-Sorcerers and hire them to try to fix Lookshy Manse and anything else that\u2019s broken, but that\u2019s dangerous and heretical on so many levels that no-one would agree to it without being hella desperate, so forget I said anything.)<br /> <br /> <br /> Ok, so I was liking Gens Amilar right up until they mentioned tactical uses of poison and disease which is ...yeah. Not that war is ever pleasant, using poison gas on a tactical level produces such horrors that anyone who doesn\u2019t regret it needs a new conscience. Granted, Creation has weapons that turn cities into glass and crystal, demons that can call forth endless night over a region, sorcerous magic that can bring life to a desert or destroy the fertility of the soil, and even native charms that can blow up a battlefield. In the face of such things, a canister of chlorine gas might almost be seen as a merciful option, I suppose. Or at least no worse.<br /> <br /> So, Karal Fire Orchid is going to be deeply embarrassing to this house, possibly to the point where the only way they can keep their status above reproach is by finding and killing her before anyone else finds out. Let\u2019s hope that the artifacts she found in the Tomb of Dreams are enough to even things up against her siblings and cousins when they come for her.<br /> <br /> So, I think my Lookshy character is going to be an Air aspect from Gens Maheka. That way I can personally push the envelope of engineering a bit without being in a family that ignores ethics in their research. I\u2019m not big on tradition, but I am big on ethics and examining the problem in depth.<br /> <br /> I suspect that you might be able to move the Maheka mountain towards the Purist stance, but it would be very difficult. Might be easier to just ...remove their seat at the table.<br /> <br /> Honestly, even if the The Gunzota Incident hasn\u2019t been considered suspicious, anyone who was involved with the conspiracy could notice how it decapitated said conspiracy and might well go \u201chmmmm.... that was effective. I wonder if we could do something like that again, on purpose?\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T09:30:20-07:00","id":1205251,"title":"","content":"The Wanasaan <br /> <br /> Ok, Jusenkyo Springs has gotten pretty metal now.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The Temple of the Reverent Whisper <br /> <br /> I love that there\u2019s a temple/bordello in Great Forks where gods can pay DBs for specific and complex ritual prayer. It is just so perfect for this game.<br /> <br /> And now I want a Zenith to start their own competing service and just see what happens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T09:30:58-07:00","id":1205252,"title":"","content":"Chapter 5<br /> <br /> Fun chapter fiction. I think it might have been previewed.<br /> <br /> I kinda want a QC writeup for Fear Eater now, just for the cool Eclipse keyword charms.<br /> <br /> Attributes and abilities are same as for solars.<br /> <br /> Dbs get five favored abilities now. Cool.<br /> <br /> Three free specialties <br /> <br /> Get two more specialties based on your background.<br /> <br /> 13 dots of merits<br /> <br /> ...and five more merit dots if you\u2019re a Dynast, Lookshian, etc. that you can spend on stuff appropriate to your station, like resources, contacts, languages, influence, etc.<br /> <br /> 15 charms to start with. Can swap them for MA charms, Evocations, and Spells as appropriate.<br /> <br /> 18 bonus points <br /> <br /> Looks like the same BP table as the core.<br /> <br /> You start with Essence 2. There\u2019s a sidebar on playing newly hatched DBs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T13:07:28-07:00","id":1205345,"title":"","content":"And here\u2019s chapter 6. No timeline on charm comments.<br /> <br /> Chapter 6<br /> <br /> Fiction is interesting. Even the patricians are considering getting in on the whole \u201cconquer the Realm\u201d thing. Which is actually a very good point. It\u2019s easy to delude oneself into thinking that the Great Houses are the only important people in the Realm, but that\u2019s not true. They have the dragon\u2019s share of the Dragon Blooded, yes, but they\u2019re also wasting their strength fighting each other. If all the patrician houses united to \u201ckeep order\u201d in the Imperial City at the right time....well. The Great Houses might have a big problem on their hands, especially if the rest of the Realm rebelled against them too. This plan is ...not bad, necessarily.<br /> <br /> Alternately, maybe they\u2019re working with Nellens too and those legions might come to their aid. Or Cathak, depending on how loyal to the empty throne they actually are.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m assuming our Monk will get chapter fiction for the MA/Sorcery chapter.<br /> <br /> Anyway<br /> <br /> Merits<br /> <br /> Notes on Corebook merits and any relevant changes. Among other things, the Dynastic stipend is Resources 3 and they note how that looks to people.<br /> <br /> Sobriquet - you\u2019re well known in Creation for your deeds and have a name that people know you by, like the Roseblack.<br /> <br /> Well-Bred is a two dot merit that grants benefits at the marriage negotiation table and Thin-Blooded is a flaw that grants penalties at said negotiation table.<br /> <br /> Sidebar on Breeding and Exaltation, giving the usual exaltation rates for couples and noting that, while merits and flaws can improve chances, there have been some wildly improbable events and it\u2019s ultimately up to the ST if a kid exalts.<br /> <br /> ....which, I suppose means I\u2019ll be nice and let all of V\u2019Neef Vala\u2019s kids Exalt. Though, maybe no wood aspects. Put that in your punnet squares and smoke it!<br /> <br /> Anyway, two page spreads.<br /> <br /> Air!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/d1EnW4kn1kg\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/d1EnW4kn1kg\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/d1EnW4kn1kg\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/d1EnW4kn1kg </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Air aspects are dreamers, visionaries, and subtle planners, always looking at what could be instead of what is. Air is the spiritual element (which is odd because Black Jade is associated with spirits). In the Kinship, they push others to be what the Air aspect knows they can be, driving towards the future.<br /> <br /> Everything seems in order. Good writing, but nothing unexpected. <br /> <br /> Earth, in contrast, is resolute, unmoved, and enduring. Stable. Calm. Firm. Unchanging. Lasting. In the Kinship, they are the pillar of stability that holds the center, keeping everyone balanced and harmonious.<br /> <br /> Air\u2019s tendency to reject tradition and Earth\u2019s tendency to uphold it seems like it would tend to drive them against each other. That said, I could see a cool dynamic where the Earth aspect keeps the Air grounded and the Air keeps the Earth from getting too stuck. Could be a great buddy cop dynamic.<br /> <br /> And now I wanna create an appearance 5 Earth Aspect who looks like an exquisite marble statue come to life.<br /> <br /> Fire is passion and intensity, If you were stoic before, you\u2019ll be emotional now, If you were passionate before, Be careful not to burn yourself out now, Anything they do, they do wholeheartedly, They are the energy that wants to spread and burn the world, That said, they can do subtle, because they are as much smoke and shadow as fire and fire can smolder unnoticed or creep into unexpected places, Stopping is what\u2019s hard for them, They\u2019re driven to do things, not to consider, contemplate, stand, wait, they gotta go, go, go, go!<br /> <br /> <br /> Given how at least three of the other elements are described as being forces of change, I\u2019ve gained new respect for the Earth aspects. If everyone else wants things to be different, just for the sake of things being different, you really do need someone to hold things together, prevent things that work from being broken, and insist on properly testing things as you go.<br /> <br /> So, water. Water moves, insinuates, creeps, it goes everywhere. If it can\u2019t go one way, it goes another, wearing new paths into places, until it reaches its destination. It conceals many things within its depths and tends to have little regard for the method of travel as long as it ultimately arrives. Morals, scruples, ethics, these things are dams for water to tunnel under, flow over, or wear down. The raging river will not stop for insurmountable obstacles, it simply flows around them. They are persistent and adaptable. They have a thousand plans and no plan, for plans are brittle and break easily. Understanding the situation and being ready to adapt invites fortune to show you the gap through which you can flow unhindered. They\u2019re troubleshooters and problem solvers who learn from failure how best to approach next time, granting these insights to their Kinship.<br /> <br /> Hmmm... Should Koyomi\u2019s hair act like she\u2019s underwater at all times? It\u2019s visually cool, but it seems like a problem for an undercover agent. Her skin should have a deep green-black tinge certainly, to signify her exceptional breeding. Also a very fluid grace to her.<br /> <br /> Wood is gardener and garden all at once. They love life, but tend to have few compunctions about returning something (or someone) to the cycle when they think it is time. They love all experiences for what they are and learn to savor everything, but likely prefer some over others. They relish opportunities for growth but like too grow in specific ways. They live, unlike the other elements, and love life but accept death.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anima Flux only kicks in at the iconic level now and only does a die of Withering damage or decisive to crashed people. Or one die of lethal per minute outside combat. If you have hardness, you\u2019re immune. Seems kinda useless now really.<br /> <br /> <br /> Being able to manipulate your element in minor ways is always fun. It\u2019s one of my favorite powers to get in any game really.<br /> <br /> Can an Air Aspect use their leap to disengage without rolling? When else would they be rolling to move?<br /> <br /> Interesting. Evocations and Sorcery costs 2 extra xp for DBs.<br /> <br /> Dragon XP is about as expected, though you can get it by RPing the Great Curse too.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Great Curse <br /> <br /> When the slain enemies of the gods pronounced their death-curse against the Exalted, the brunt of it fell upon the Solars who led the Divine Revolution. The Dragon-Blooded were still accursed, but to a much lesser degree. Consequently, unlike the Solars and other Exalted, Dragon-Blooded don\u2019t possess a Limit track or experience Limit Break. While the Great Curse still influences their behavior, its manifestations are determined solely by the player of a Dragon-Blooded character. <br /> <br /> Roleplaying the Great Curse well is rewarded with Dragon Experience (p. XX). However, while a Dragon-Blood\u2019s excesses or warped judgment might cause problems for her fellow characters, it\u2019s never an excuse to ruin other players\u2019 fun at the table. If a dramatic moment caused by the Great Curse isn\u2019t something that the entire group can appreciate, it doesn\u2019t award Dragon Experience. <br /> <br /> The Great Curse manifests differently in each elemental Aspect of Dragon-Blooded: <br /> <br /> \u2022 Air Aspects: An Air Aspect\u2019s Great Curse can lead her to react with excessive anger, frustration, or despair when the world fails to live up to her idealistic visions of it. She may become so caught up in her high-minded idealism that she ignores the consequences it has for others or the suffering that it causes, or hold such confidence in her intellect and vision that she\u2019ll brook no insult without retribution, or take truly foolish risks not believing that she could be wrong. <br /> <br /> \u2022 Earth Aspects: An Earth Aspect\u2019s Great Curse may render her ruthless or cruel in defense of her cherished institutions and traditions, or leave her single-minded and immutable, refusing all counsel and closing her heart. She may respond to any insult or challenge to an important tradition with earthshaking anger or abject despair. <br /> <br /> \u2022 Fire Aspects: A Fire Aspect\u2019s Great Curse intensifies her emotions and desires to the point of dangerous excess. Depending on the circumstances, she might be overcome with overwhelming zeal for her cause, self-hatred over any imperfection she displays, reckless fury against hated foes or in defense of those she loves, or self-sacrificing despair when those she loves suffer. <br /> <br /> \u2022 Water Aspects: A Water Aspect\u2019s Great Curse makes her perseverance a liability as she goes to unnecessary extremes to overcome obstacles or protect allies, or faces down impossible obstacles refusing to believe she can be defeated. She might take any underhanded shortcut or employ any plans, no matter how convoluted, in the pursuit of her own triumph. <br /> <br /> \u2022 Wood Aspects: A Wood Aspect\u2019s Great Curse might intensify her sensuality into hedonistic excess, dangerous thrill-seeking, or wild binges that leave her overcome by guilt, regret, or the desire to atone. She may instead become overzealous in her attempts to nurture the people and societies around her, becoming overbearingly controlling of that which she protects or mercilessly pruning away undesirable elements. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T01:31:45-07:00","id":1206822,"title":"","content":"Chapter 7<br /> <br /> Nice to see more of Novia. I like her.<br /> <br /> I would know more of Glafira.<br /> <br /> Mnemon... is arrogant and dismissive, but I do like that she is rebuilding this place rather than leaving it to suffer or wither. I would have liked some regret for her satrap\u2019s part in this whole thing, but you don\u2019t have a lot of words available in these things, so it\u2019s ok.<br /> <br /> Now. Charms.<br /> <br /> Hmm. If you can build special MA styles to interact with Aura mechanics, why can\u2019t you build more of them or artifacts or anything specifically to interact with Aura mechanics? Or can you, if you do it on purpose?<br /> <br /> <br /> Archery<br /> <br /> Ok, so. My understanding is this.<br /> <br /> I can combo Unobstructed Hunter\u2019s Aim, Sky-Calming Draw, and Life-Swelling Sap Strike to make a distract gambit out to long range, but I have to aim first and I don\u2019t end up with an aura at the end of my turn.<br /> <br /> Is the aim action needed to make a shot at medium+ range distinct from the one needed for Sky-Calming Draw? If not, if I\u2019m in Air Aura, does that mean I can use Sky-Calming Draw to shoot people without aiming?<br /> <br /> Arbor Sentinel Technique is very cool.<br /> <br /> If I combo Drawing Lightning Style and Sky-Calming Draw, do I still have to spend an action aiming?<br /> <br /> Would an upgrade that let you apply Dragonfly Finds Mate to ranged attacks targeting people in close range of you, or short if they\u2019re Sworn Kin, be ok?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> In previous editions, Swallows Defend the Nest let you defend against lots of ranged attacks. Would a charm that let you defend other using half your dex+archery against ranged attacks for any allies in close range be ok? Maybe it provokes an ammo check too?<br /> <br /> ....ok, just saw Seven Year Swarm Volley. Never mind.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m a little confused why Arrow Rain Tempest is a Water charm sitting deep in a tree full of Wood charms. I\u2019m assuming it\u2019s because the charm is absurdly powerful, so making it amazingly difficult to set up is necessary, but is that the actual reason?<br /> <br /> <br /> So, it looks like the Air archer is a sniper who can put a perfectly aimed arrow nearly anywhere they want on the battlefield at ranges that are simply ludicrous.<br /> <br /> The Wood Archer, on the other hand, will never run out of ammo and likes to prove their bounty by sending as much of it down range as quickly as possible. They become as a machine gun nest/defense system. Because they can also become a missile defense system at high essence.<br /> <br /> Other elements are good for a few tricks, Fire has a couple of Firewand charms that are usually also Wood aspected, but this ability is mostly Wood with some Air.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.nuklearpower.com/2009/01/27/episode-1087-exalted-feat/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.nuklearpower.com/comics/8-bit-theater/090127.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.nuklearpower.com/2009/01/27/episode-1087-exalted-feat/\" target=\"_blank\"> Nuklear Power &raquo; Archive &raquo; Episode 1087: Exalted Feat </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.nuklearpower.com/2009/01/27/episode-1087-exalted-feat/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.nuklearpower.com/2009/01/27/episode-1087-exalted-feat/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T08:23:31-07:00","id":1206887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200185-brilliantrain-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1206822#post1206822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would have liked some regret for her satrap\u2019s part in this whole thing, but you don\u2019t have a lot of words available in these things, so it\u2019s ok.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b&quot;I regret that you aligned with an Anathema and rebelled in a manner that forced me to tear down your blasphemous and conceited towers.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you can build special MA styles to interact with Aura mechanics, why can\u2019t you build more of them or artifacts or anything specifically to interact with Aura mechanics? Or can you, if you do it on purpose?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI suppose that a Martial Art based on emulation of an Immaculate/Elemental Dragon gets a special dispensation there, when nothing else would.<br /> <br /> Or are the Dragon Styles supposed to be a special refinement of the Dragon Blooded Essence?<br /> <br /> \u200bSurely we'll get the answer when we have the Martial Arts chapter, and I imagine it will be something credibly unique to those particular styles.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m a little confused why Arrow Rain Tempest is a Water charm sitting deep in a tree full of Wood charms. I\u2019m assuming it\u2019s because the charm is absurdly powerful, so making it amazingly difficult to set up is necessary, but is that the actual reason?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI think that in a few cases, the Element of a Charm was as simple as &quot;what does the effect of this Charm look like&quot;. It's a Charm to make it rain arrows, hence, Water.<br /> <br /> \u200bEvery Charm of a different element besides the Signatures is interspersed through Charms with the element of the Ability's associated Aspect.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T08:40:48-07:00","id":1206896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200185-brilliantrain-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1206887#post1206887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b&quot;I regret that you aligned with an Anathema and rebelled in a manner that forced me to tear down your blasphemous and conceited towers.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see any indication that the satrap herself rebelled; a satrap is not a prince.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T09:18:57-07:00","id":1206909,"title":"","content":"I was more bemused by the image of Mnemon feeling regret about correcting a wayward satrapy. I'm not actually sure myself what BrilliantRain meant by &quot;the satrap's part in this&quot;. The quote was meant as something directed towards Jiara, not Mnemon's subordinate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T10:07:42-07:00","id":1206929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200185-brilliantrain-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1206896#post1206896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see any indication that the satrap herself rebelled; a satrap is not a prince.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some of the background we had before indicated that Jianara's Mnemon Satrap basically decided that the best way to get the artifacts under Jiara's capital city was to bulldoze the most ancient and respected places in the city, some of which might have been designed by Mnemon herself. This decision did not go over well with the populace and eventually resulted in Perfect Soul's Exaltation.<br /> <br /> All I was referring to was that I'd have enjoyed finding out what she did to that idiot, but this particular bit of fiction was not really the time nor place for it.<br /> <br /> That's also assuming the backstory remains true.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T11:23:26-07:00","id":1206959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200185-brilliantrain-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1206929#post1206929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">some of which might have been designed by Mnemon herself.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really see that. Mnemon seems to have nothing but contempt for the native architecture; I can't imagine her seeing its demolition in the course of extracting resources for the House as anything other than a bonus.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">All I was referring to was that I'd have enjoyed finding out what she did to that idiot</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI feel as though that would be the same logic of &quot;sorry you were so offended&quot; response. Like, unless one took the Perfect Soul write-up to suggest that the Mnemon representatives went about it in an especially cloddish manner, exploitation of the satrapies is literally what they're there for.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T12:03:54-07:00","id":1206975,"title":"","content":"All of the architecture Mnemon is knocking over to get at the newly-discovered artifact stores predates House Mnemon and, I suspect, the Great Contagion itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T12:52:39-07:00","id":1206990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200185-brilliantrain-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1206959#post1206959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't really see that. Mnemon seems to have nothing but contempt for the native architecture; I can't imagine her seeing its demolition in the course of extracting resources for the House as anything other than a bonus.<br /> <br /> \u200bI feel as though that would be the same logic of &quot;sorry you were so offended&quot; response. Like, unless one took the Perfect Soul write-up to suggest that the Mnemon representatives went about it in an especially cloddish manner, exploitation of the satrapies is literally what they're there for.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/notes/john-m%C3%B8rke/a-look-at-exalteds-new-solars-perfect-soul/10153822735365909\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://static.xx.fbcdn.net/rsrc.php/y8/r/dF5SId3UHWd.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/notes/john-m%C3%B8rke/a-look-at-exalteds-new-solars-perfect-soul/10153822735365909\" target=\"_blank\"> Log into Facebook </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/notes/john-m%C3%B8rke/a-look-at-exalteds-new-solars-perfect-soul/10153822735365909\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.facebook.com/notes/john-m%C3%B8rke/a-look-at-exalteds-new-solars-perfect-soul/10153822735365909 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Log into Facebook to start sharing and connecting with your friends, family, and people you know. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Jiara has long been a subject state of the Realm, complete with a governing satrap, making the Khidara nobility little more than a puppet. In recent times, House Mnemon has forced hard taxes on the Jiaran people, with brutal consequences for withholding. This problem only intensified in the last five years, when extensive First Age ruins were discovered around and beneath Jiara.<br /> <br /> The satrap Mnemon Jerof incensed the people by turning families out of their homes to tear up streets and buildings. Temples were even demolished to get at the ruins, an act that served to cow the gods rather than stir them to wrath\u2014but only with the help of Immaculate Monks who moved to intervene, no thanks to Satrap Jerof.<br /> <br /> Rather than conduct discrete surveys with local temple authorities, Jerof decimated ancient spiritual centers for the Jiaran people. Rather than order the princes of Jiara to host people displaced by excavations, he seized the properties of those whose land was suspected to be above ruins and gave those estates over to sycophantic patricians from the Realm. When the people began to stir with unrest, Satrap Jerof set a garrison inside the city, enacted a curfew, and began forcing any Jiaran protester or any citizen in violation of curfew to work on the excavation of Jiaran holy sites.<br /> <br /> Because Jerof employed experts of dubious ability to head the excavations, and because he under-budgeted and rushed the works, the excavation went disastrously more often than not. Dig sites were often in the wrong places, temples torn down for no reason, while other ruins were buried in collapses triggered by careless engineers. </div> </div> </div> &quot;Cloddish&quot; doesn't really begin to describe it honestly. That said, I dunno if that's all still accurate or not, since it's from John Morke's notes and not official text in a game book or anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T15:05:17-07:00","id":1207026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200185-brilliantrain-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1206990#post1206990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Cloddish&quot; doesn't really begin to describe it honestly. That said, I dunno if that's all still accurate or not, since it's from John Morke's notes and not official text in a game book or anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably not very accurate at all, considering this is a facebook post and Eric clarified the Satrap is a women a couple of posts above you.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/223-calboon","name":"Calboon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar223_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T15:54:38-07:00","id":1207041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200185-brilliantrain-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1206990#post1206990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Cloddish&quot; doesn't really begin to describe it honestly.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bYeah, I can't tell you how many British officials were given a very stern telling off when they responded to Irish unrest with things like suspension of civil liberties and mass imprisonment without trial.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T16:07:36-07:00","id":1207047,"title":"","content":"&quot;If they don't obey your lawful orders, apply force. If that doesn't work, escalate force, and continue escalating until they do or until they cease to be a factor.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T18:00:47-07:00","id":1207088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200185-brilliantrain-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1207041#post1207041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bYeah, I can't tell you how many British officials were given a very stern telling off when they responded to Irish unrest with things like suspension of civil liberties and mass imprisonment without trial.</div> </div> </div> </div>For the chapter fiction in question it doesn't even really describe the whole Jiaran rebellion and hunt for artifacts so it's totally unreasonable to assume we'd get all of Mnemon's feelings on the matter but I think you're misunderstanding what Brilliant Rain is saying.<br /> <br /> It's more a matter of being sloppy than being immoral. Like yeah you got the artifacts, good job, but you made a mess doing it. Not because you had to, because you're dumb. Next time remember you're from my house, and that means you're a professional who hires professionals. Seriously though good job getting those artifacts. Meanwhile the satrap is sitting there wondering why, apparently, they can't do anything right.<br /> <br /> It's not unreasonable since she's an architect and those temples are shogunate era construction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T18:38:48-07:00","id":1207106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200185-brilliantrain-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1207088#post1207088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you're misunderstanding what Brilliant Rain is saying.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bIt looks to me like saying that Mnemon would tell off her representative for having not sufficiently taken the feelings of mortals into account.<br /> <br /> \u200bAnd, well, I think Mnemon is a more well-rounded person in this Edition, but that fiction piece is pretty explicitly depicting her as somebody who has become largely inured to their existence and seeing them mostly in terms of patterns fulfilling their place in the Perfected Hierarchy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not unreasonable since she's an architect and those temples are shogunate era construction.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bBut the fiction outright depicts her as thinking poorly of their stuff.<br /> <br /> \u200b&quot;Mnemon-sama, reports are saying that caches of First Age magic have been discovered beneath the vulgar, conceited buildings of the Jiarans. I propose that we tear them down in order to acquire those magics for the House, so that we might reconstruct their city in accordance with proper Immaculate fashions and principles, and make them pay us for the privilege.&quot;<br /> \u200b&quot;Ah yes, the much coveted win-win-win.&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T20:41:41-07:00","id":1207144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200185-brilliantrain-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1207106#post1207106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bIt looks to me like saying that Mnemon would tell off her representative for having not sufficiently taken the feelings of mortals into account.<br /> <br /> \u200bAnd, well, I think Mnemon is a more well-rounded person in this Edition, but that fiction piece is pretty explicitly depicting her as somebody who has become largely inured to their existence and seeing them mostly in terms of patterns fulfilling their place in the Perfected Hierarchy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah no, totally screw the mortals, that doesn't mean you've got an excuse for wasting money and ruining the satrapy. Like if I task my butler with getting rid of an ant infestation, and he hires a guy that C-4s my lawn I can't tell you how few fucks I give for the lives of actual insects but seriously next time don't hire a guy that's so clearly incompetent. There's no room in the perfected hierarchy for words like &quot;Rushed, under-budget, disastrous, or careless&quot;.<br /> <br /> To be even more clear, if you tear down a temple for no reason, you spent a ton of silver, manpower, time, and riled up the locals* for a strict loss and no gain. If you bury an excavation because you were careless you better not have lost any engineers doing it. Not because of some emotional attachment to the hard working women that put the thing together, but because engineers are friggin expensive and not that common. If they had to do it then fine, but they clearly didn't. It's not about making sacrifices for greater gains it's about being ham-fisted when you could have been precise.<br /> <br /> If you tear up the streets, lock down a satrapy, provoke a rebellion, waste money, waste lives (Purely pragmatic, not saying Mnemon would care about death if the people weren't on her payroll), and find awesome equipment in the process, then good, but better is expected.<br /> <br /> And just because I know people will somehow read that and think I'm advocating for a kind, compassionate Mnemon who sheds a single womanly tear for the suffering of her people, I'll say again that this is not about showing empathy for peasants, it's about acting in a way that is clean, efficient and productive. The funny thing is even with THAT sentence people will still misunderstand.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1200185-brilliantrain-reads-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought?p=1207106#post1207106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bBut the fiction outright depicts her as thinking poorly of their stuff.<br /> <br /> \u200b&quot;Mnemon-sama, reports are saying that caches of First Age magic have been discovered beneath the vulgar, conceited buildings of the Jiarans. I propose that we tear them down in order to acquire those magics for the House, so that we might reconstruct their city in accordance with proper Immaculate fashions and principles, and make them pay us for the privilege.&quot;<br /> \u200b&quot;Ah yes, the much coveted win-win-win.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah that's true, although it does seem inconsistent with them being Shogunate era temples. It's not like mortals were running the place during the Shogunate. I THINK what it means is since the Shogunate ended the people of Jiara tried to do that, by then it'd be mortal controlled, that stuff would be newer than the temples though.<br /> <br /> <br /> *Not that you care about the feelings of mortals, but Mnemon isn't a defense contractor. When she has to go put down a rebellion she doesn't make profit off it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T18:32:05-07:00","id":1207471,"title":"","content":"Athletics<br /> <br /> Base excellency adds successes to the roll. Odd.<br /> <br /> Is the storyteller\u2019s guide going to have an athletics system in it or are we just assuming that \u201crolling to jump\u201d is a thing?<br /> <br /> I\u2019m a little confused why Perfect Climbing Attitude is back here. Is it supposed to be Essence 2?<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve noted that the Signature charms of elements that are not common in that ability tend to lack the Aura keyword. Which means they can be comboed freely, as long as you don\u2019t mind getting kicked out of Aura.<br /> <br /> Does the swimming booster charm let you breathe underwater, if you don\u2019t already?<br /> <br /> The Fire aspect runs you down. They are inescapable and trying to flee will likely end with you on fire.<br /> <br /> The Earth aspect is stronk like bull! <br /> <br /> The other elements are pretty much just there to help you out in whatever environment is most appropriate to them.<br /> <br /> <br /> Awareness <br /> <br /> If my character is blind, can I use Feeling the Dragon\u2019s Bones to negate most combat penalties for fighting while blind? Would you consider it reasonable for my character to be able to just have it going indefinitely, provided they never used non-Earth charms? Or would that need an upgrade charm?<br /> <br /> Would an upgrade to All-Encompassing Earth Sense that let you keep the Air or Water versions up while in the appropriate Aura work? Maybe let the Air one work in non-enclosed spaces and the Water one work in mist/fog/gentle rain too?<br /> <br /> What effect does Dragon\u2019s Crushing Gaze actually have? Say there\u2019s a stealthy person spying on me, I use this charm, I win the roll and now they lose one success. But...that doesn\u2019t help me, because I won the roll already. Do other people get to reroll? Or are we supposed to remember the rolls everyone else got and they retroactively win if they only missed by one? How does it work?<br /> <br /> I think Fire\u2019s thing is exploding 10s. Wood\u2019s thing looks like it might be removing penalties. Earth\u2019s thing seems like it\u2019s adding successes. Not sure about air or water yet.<br /> <br /> Eye of Blazing Truth. Maybe you should skip hiding in cardboard boxes when DBs are looking for you.<br /> <br /> Ok, so I get that these charms are useful, appropriate, and thematic, but the first three Signature Water charms are only useful if you\u2019re in the water. I feel like Water Aspects are being pigeonholed as Aquaman.<br /> <br /> Maybe it\u2019ll be better once I get into brawl.<br /> <br /> That said, Serpent-of-the-Depths Discernment does seem like it\u2019d be fairly handy in any garden with an unexpectedly deep ornamental koi pond. At least until the other DBs twig to that trick anyway.<br /> <br /> Ok, Sense the Hidden Ember is cool.<br /> <br /> The earth is watching.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T22:58:04-07:00","id":1208330,"title":"","content":"Ok, so, rather than simply make meme references and funny comments, I've decided to do something useful and create a <i>spreadsheet.</i><br /> <br /> No, seriously.<br /> <br /> I've got the names of every DB charm in there and spaces to note what element it is and places to flag the new keywords and everything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1LUZ_ub0LW60-Q5Xf0z3LPTLIgPbwT5USj-re8Pa5LFs/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1LUZ_ub0LW60-Q5Xf0z3LPTLIgPbwT5USj-re8Pa5LFs/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1LUZ_ub0LW60-Q5Xf0z3LPTLIgPbwT5USj-re8Pa5LFs/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1LUZ_ub0LW60-Q5Xf0z3LPTLIgPbwT5USj-re8Pa5LFs/edit?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I only have the info filled out for Archery so far, but I'll try to continue adding more in. I also made it editable by anyone with that link, should people wish to help. If you do wish to help, please use the way Archery was done and formatted as a guide.<br /> <br /> Once done, sort and filter operations should make it easy to find, say, all the Non-Aura Starting Water charms or all the Signature charms with No Prereqs, and help you figure out how best to go for a particular DB build.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T14:08:16-07:00","id":1217110,"title":"","content":"So, any progress on this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-09T16:58:56-07:00","id":1217191,"title":"","content":"Between a vacation and finals I haven\u2019t really had much chance to work on it. That said a very nice person added in pretty much everything but the elements of each charm, so I should be able to finish this next week. Alternately, if anyone else wants to finish it sooner, they may do so. Or make a copy and change the formatting around if they think of a better method.<br /> <br /> One thing I did do was to record the number of charms in each ability on the second page. Performance has the most at 30, then Larceny with 28, followed by Melee with 25. Stealth has the fewest at 15, then Dodge at 16.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":226,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","user":"BrilliantRain","date":". 05-09-2018, 08:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}